39", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Decomposition Milestones Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ra2TXGNBM1FK2cFNDE7PnD', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/decomposition_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ra2TXGNBM1FK2cFNDE7PnD', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Overview\\nTransform the Ensemble AI Executive Director from a simple coordinator into an intelligent planner with a Smart Task Decomposition Engine.\\n\\n## Milestone 1: Core Decomposition Engine (Priority)\\n**Objective**: Build the core TaskDecompositionEngine class with all essential methods.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_engine.py` - Core engine with:\\n  - `TaskDecompositionEngine` class\\n  - `analyze_task()` - Analyze task complexity and domain\\n  - `decompose_task()` - Break task into sub-tasks\\n  - `generate_dependency_graph()` - Create DAG using NetworkX\\n  - `estimate_resources()` - Calculate agent/cost/time estimates\\n  - `optimize_allocation()` - Linear programming for optimal allocation\\n  - `generate_execution_schedule()` - Create parallel execution waves\\n- Pydantic data models: TaskAnalysis, SubTask, DecompositionPlan, ResourceEstimate, AllocationPlan, Schedule\\n- Unit tests for core functionality\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Engine can analyze and decompose a complex task into valid DAG\\n- Resource estimates include agents, tokens, cost, and time\\n- Execution schedule produces valid parallel waves\\n- All tests pass\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Learning Module\\n**Objective**: Build the DecompositionLearner for continuous improvement.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_learner.py` - Learning module with:\\n  - `DecompositionLearner` class\\n  - `record_execution()` - Store actual vs. estimated performance\\n  - `improve_estimates()` - Calibrate estimates based on history\\n  - `suggest_improvements()` - Generate optimization suggestions\\n  - `get_historical_accuracy()` - Report on estimate accuracy\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Learning module integrates with existing metrics.py database\\n- Calibration improves estimates over multiple executions\\n- Accuracy metrics properly tracked\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: API Endpoints & Backend Integration\\n**Objective**: Add REST API endpoints for decomposition.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `POST /api/decompose` - Decompose a user request\\n- `POST /api/approve-plan` - Accept/reject/modify plan\\n- `GET /api/decomposition-history` - Get historical accuracy\\n- Integration with existing backend main.py\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All endpoints return correct JSON responses\\n- Error handling for invalid requests\\n- CORS configured properly\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1, Milestone 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Frontend Visualization\\n**Objective**: Build React component for task decomposition visualization.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx` component with:\\n  - Mermaid diagram rendering for dependency graph\\n  - Resource estimates display (agents, cost, time)\\n  - Execution wave visualization\\n  - Agent assignment table\\n  - Approve/Reject/Modify action buttons\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Component renders decomposition plans correctly\\n- User can approve/reject/modify plans\\n- Responsive design works on various screens\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 3\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 5: Testing & Documentation\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive test suite and documentation.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `tests/test_decomposition.py` - Full test suite:\\n  - Unit tests for each method\\n  - Integration tests for full flow\\n  - Graph validity tests (DAG, cycles)\\n  - Benchmark tests (simple/medium/complex)\\n  - Learning accuracy tests\\n- `TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md` - Documentation:\\n  - Architecture overview\\n  - Usage examples\\n  - API reference\\n  - Configuration options\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Test coverage > 80%\\n- All tests pass\\n- Documentation complete and accurate\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1-4\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n- Milestone 1: Core Engine - ~2-3 hours\\n- Milestone 2: Learning Module - ~1-2 hours\\n- Milestone 3: API Endpoints - ~1 hour\\n- Milestone 4: Frontend - ~1-2 hours\\n- Milestone 5: Testing & Docs - ~1-2 hours\\n\\n**Total Estimated Time**: ~6-10 hours of agent work\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014dSpX3g8EmWAhEgRHrctQR', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Requirements Document\n\n## Project Overview\n\n**Vision**: Transform the Ensemble AI Executive Director from a simple coordinator into an intelligent planner with a Smart Task Decomposition Engine.\n\n**Objective**: Build a sophisticated task decomposition system that analyzes complex user requests, breaks them into optimal sub-tasks, generates dependency graphs, estimates resources, and creates efficient execution schedules.\n\n## Core Requirements\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n**F1. Task Analysis & Decomposition**\n- System must analyze task complexity and domain\n- Break complex tasks into manageable sub-tasks\n- Generate directed acyclic graphs (DAG) for task dependencies\n- Support parallel execution planning\n\n**F2. Resource Management**\n- Estimate required agents, tokens, cost, and time for each sub-task\n- Optimize resource allocation using linear programming\n- Generate execution schedules with parallel waves\n- Support multiple agent types and specializations\n\n**F3. Learning & Improvement**\n- Record actual vs. estimated performance data\n- Continuously improve estimates based on historical data\n- Track accuracy metrics over time\n- Suggest optimization improvements\n\n**F4. API Integration**\n- Provide REST endpoints for decomposition operations\n- Support plan approval/rejection/modification workflows\n- Integrate with existing FastAPI backend\n- Maintain CORS compatibility\n\n**F5. User Interface**\n- Visualize dependency graphs using Mermaid diagrams\n- Display resource estimates and execution schedules\n- Provide interactive plan approval interface\n- Show agent assignments and timeline\n\n### Non-Functional Requirements\n\n**N1. Performance**\n- Decomposition analysis must complete within 5 seconds\n- Support concurrent decomposition requests\n- Maintain response time under 2 seconds for API calls\n\n**N2. Reliability**\n- System must handle invalid inputs gracefully\n- Provide meaningful error messages\n- Maintain data integrity across operations\n\n**N3. Scalability**\n- Support task graphs with up to 100 nodes\n- Handle multiple concurrent users\n- Efficient memory usage for large decompositions\n\n**N4. Maintainability**\n- Test coverage > 80%\n- Comprehensive documentation\n- Clean, modular architecture\n\n## Technical Specifications\n\n### Technology Stack\n- **Backend**: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic\n- **Dependencies**: NetworkX (graph operations), PuLP (optimization)\n- **Frontend**: React, Mermaid (diagram rendering)\n- **Database**: SQLite (existing metrics.py integration)\n- **Testing**: pytest\n\n### Data Models\n\n**TaskAnalysis**\n- task_id: str\n- complexity: str (simple|medium|complex)\n- domain: str\n- estimated_duration: float\n- confidence_score: float\n\n**SubTask**\n- sub_task_id: str\n- description: str\n- agent_type: str\n- dependencies: List[str]\n- estimated_resources: ResourceEstimate\n\n**DecompositionPlan**\n- plan_id: str\n- original_task: str\n- sub_tasks: List[SubTask]\n- dependency_graph: dict\n- total_estimate: ResourceEstimate\n- execution_schedule: Schedule\n\n### API Endpoints\n\n**POST /api/decompose**\n- Input: user request text\n- Output: DecompositionPlan JSON\n- Functionality: Analyze and decompose task\n\n**POST /api/approve-plan**\n- Input: plan_id, approval_status, modifications\n- Output: execution status\n- Functionality: Process plan approval/rejection\n\n**GET /api/decomposition-history**\n- Input: optional filters\n- Output: historical accuracy metrics\n- Functionality: Retrieve learning data\n\n### File Structure\n\n```\nsrc/runtime/agents/\n├── decomposition_engine.py     # Core TaskDecompositionEngine\n├── decomposition_learner.py    # Learning and improvement module\n\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/backend/\n├── main.py                     # Updated with new endpoints\n\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/\n├── TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx # React visualization component\n\ntests/\n├── test_decomposition.py       # Comprehensive test suite\n\ndocs/\n├── TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md      # Architecture and usage docs\n```\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n**Primary Success**\n- Core engine can decompose complex tasks into valid DAGs\n- Resource estimates are generated for all components\n- Learning module improves estimate accuracy over time\n- Frontend provides clear visualization and interaction\n- All tests pass with >80% coverage\n\n**Quality Gates**\n- No circular dependencies in generated graphs\n- Resource estimates within 20% accuracy after learning\n- API response times under 2 seconds\n- UI components are responsive and accessible\n- Complete documentation with examples\n\n## Assumptions\n\n**Technical Assumptions**\n- Existing Ensemble AI infrastructure is stable\n- FastAPI backend can handle additional endpoints\n- React frontend supports Mermaid diagram rendering\n- NetworkX library provides adequate graph operations\n\n**Business Assumptions**\n- Users will engage with decomposition plans before execution\n- Historical data will improve estimate accuracy\n- Linear programming approach is suitable for resource optimization\n- DAG structure is appropriate for task dependencies\n\n## Constraints\n\n**Time Constraints**\n- Implementation targeted for 6-10 hours of development work\n- Must integrate with existing system without breaking changes\n\n**Technical Constraints**\n- Must use existing database schema (metrics.py)\n- Frontend must maintain current design patterns\n- Backend must preserve existing API compatibility\n\n**Resource Constraints**\n- Development limited to specified agent capabilities\n- Must work within current infrastructure limits\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Real-time collaboration on decomposition plans\n- Advanced machine learning for task prediction\n- Integration with external project management tools\n- Automated task execution (only planning)\n- Multi-tenant support\n\n## Risk Analysis\n\n**High Risk**\n- Graph complexity causing performance issues\n- Learning algorithm convergence problems\n\n**Medium Risk**\n- Frontend rendering large dependency graphs\n- API integration compatibility issues\n\n**Low Risk**\n- Data model changes\n- Testing infrastructure setup\n\n## Implementation Methodology\n\n**Development Approach**: Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n1. Write tests first for each component\n2. Implement code to pass tests\n3. Refactor for optimization\n4. Integration testing between components\n\n**Quality Assurance**\n- Unit tests for all core methods\n- Integration tests for full workflows\n- Performance benchmarking\n- User acceptance testing for UI components'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014dSpX3g8EmWAhEgRHrctQR', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_015735.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260116_015735.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012cUYKg632234pd7Gi9udRY', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'e377745c', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements analysis complete. Created comprehensive requirements document from decomposition_milestones.md. Project scope: Build Smart Task Decomposition Engine with 5 milestones covering core engine, learning module, API endpoints, frontend visualization, and testing/documentation.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012cUYKg632234pd7Gi9udRY', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014cyj8YDrUV75U7hFfjSLvf', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'e377745c', 'description': 'Implement Smart Task Decomposition Engine with TDD methodology - 5 milestones: Core Engine, Learning Module, API Endpoints, Frontend Visualization, Testing & Documentation', 'assigned_to': 'development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014cyj8YDrUV75U7hFfjSLvf', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "6d7b609e", "message": "Added task: Implement Smart Task Decomposition Engine with TDD methodology - 5 milestones: Core Engine, Learning Module, API Endpoints, Frontend Visualization, Testing & Documentation"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid