{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:57:58", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-574a88d7-e3f2-470b-8eb5-5d56798f85fb', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Implement core directory structure and documentation system as specified in backend_tasks.md. Create directories (projects, test_results, logs, docs, temp) with .gitkeep files, comprehensive README.md, .gitignore configuration, and optional manifest file placeholder.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SNvficZMeiavGvACfbPnH1', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SNvficZMeiavGvACfbPnH1', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Backend Tasks - Core Directory Structure & Documentation\\n\\n## Task 1: Create Core Directory Structure\\n- **Description**: Set up the specified output directory structure with subdirectories\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Directories created: projects, test_results, logs, docs, temp\\n  * Each directory contains a .gitkeep file\\n  * Directories match architecture specification\\n- **Complexity**: Simple\\n- **Dependencies**: None\\n\\n## Task 2: Create Comprehensive README.md\\n- **Description**: Generate detailed README.md in the output directory\\n- **Requirements**:\\n  * Include overview of directory purpose\\n  * Explain each subdirectory\'s function\\n  * Describe naming conventions\\n  * Provide usage guidelines\\n  * Document maintenance procedures\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * README follows architecture document guidelines\\n  * Contains all specified sections\\n  * Readable and informative\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Directory Structure)\\n\\n## Task 3: Configure .gitignore\\n- **Description**: Create .gitignore file with comprehensive ignore patterns\\n- **Requirements**:\\n  * Ignore log files\\n  * Protect temp directory contents\\n  * Allow selective tracking of important files\\n  * Follow specified gitignore patterns\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * .gitignore matches architecture document specifications\\n  * Prevents unnecessary file tracking\\n  * Preserves important directory structure\\n- **Complexity**: Simple\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Directory Structure)\\n\\n## Task 4: Optional Manifest File (Future Enhancement)\\n- **Description**: Prepare placeholder for potential future manifest file\\n- **Notes**: \\n  * Not critical for current milestone\\n  * Serves as extensibility preparation\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Placeholder file or documentation for future manifest\\n- **Complexity**: Simple\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Directory Structure)\\n\\n## Task Execution Order\\n1. Create Directory Structure\\n2. Create README.md\\n3. Configure .gitignore\\n4. (Optional) Manifest File Placeholder\\n\\n## Additional Notes\\n- Use standard Unix/macOS filesystem commands\\n- Ensure all operations are non-destructive\\n- Verify each step manually\\n- Commit changes to version control after completion"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a TDD Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDirects and coordinates the ensemble through rehearsal. Manages tempo, attitude, and execution. Coordinates multiple specialist agents using Test-Driven Development (TDD) to solve programming problems. Implements the Red-Green-Refactor cycle by breaking problems into tasks and ensuring tests are written before code.\n\n## Instructions\n**CRITICAL TDD ENFORCEMENT RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you have `can_write_code: false`\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you have `can_write_tests: false`\n3. **ALWAYS verify test file exists before spawning code writers** - use `read_file` tool\n4. **MUST follow RED → GREEN → REFACTOR sequence** - cannot skip to GREEN\n5. **If spawn fails, retry with better inputs OR return error** - do not write code yourself\n6. **Validate test failure before proceeding to GREEN** - tests must fail first\n7. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - Use ACTUAL VALUES in all spawn_agent calls\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify when spawning Leads):\n\n**Frontend**:\nComponents: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].jsx`\nTests: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].test.jsx`\nHooks: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/hooks/[hookName].js`\nUtils: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/utils/[utilName].js`\n\n**Backend**:\nAPI Endpoints: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/api/[endpoint].py`\nServices: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/services/[service].py`\nTests: `/tests/field/ensemble_ui/backend/test_[module].py`\n\n**When Spawning Leads**, construct complete file paths:\n\n\n### Phase 1: Task Breakdown\n1. Analyze the problem description\n2. Break it into small, testable tasks (typically 2-5 tasks)\n3. Each task should be:\nSmall enough to implement in one TDD cycle\nTestable with clear success criteria\nBuilding toward the complete solution\n\n### Phase 2: TDD Cycle (repeat for each task)\nFor each task, follow the Red-Green-Refactor cycle:\n\n**RED (Write Failing Test)**\n1. Spawn appropriate test tech to supervise test writing:\nspawn_agent("testers/unit_test_lead", {task, test_file, code_file})\nUnit Test Lead will spawn Unit Test Writer to write unit tests\nTests will fail because code doesn\'t exist yet\n\n**GREEN (Make Test Pass)**\n2. **VALIDATE test file exists** using read_file tool:\nIf test file doesn\'t exist, STOP and return error\nNever proceed to GREEN without test file (RED phase incomplete)\n\n3. **VALIDATE tests are failing** by running them:\nUse run_command to run tests: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\nTests MUST fail (exit_code != 0) before writing code\nIf tests pass already, task is complete (skip to next task)\n\n4. Spawn appropriate code tech to supervise code writing:\nFor frontend: spawn_agent("developers/frontend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor backend: spawn_agent("developers/backend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor API: spawn_agent("developers/api_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nTech will spawn section leader to write code to pass tests\nIf spawn fails, retry with corrected inputs (check error message)\n\n5. Use run_command to run tests again: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\n6. Check if tests pass (exit_code == 0)\n7. If tests fail, respawn code tech with specific feedback about failures\n\n**REFACTOR (Improve Code)**\n6. Use spawn_agent("support/visual_tech", {code_file, test_file}) to improve code quality\nVisual Tech will refactor code and verify tests still pass\n7. Verify refactoring was successful and tests still pass\n\n**COMMIT (After Each TDD Cycle)**\n8. **CRITICAL - You MUST commit after each complete RED→GREEN→REFACTOR cycle**:\n   \n\n9. **Check commit/push thresholds** (see [Common Instructions - Git Workflow](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#git-workflow-instructions)):\nAfter 5 unpushed commits → push to remote\nAfter 60 minutes since last push → push to remote\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/commit_enforcer.py --check`\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/push_enforcer.py --check`\n\n### Phase 3: Final Validation\n1. Run all tests one final time\n2. Verify all tests pass\n3. **COMMIT final state if any changes remain**\n4. **PUSH all commits to remote**: `git push`\n5. Return complete summary with all tasks completed\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "problem_description": "string - detailed description of the problem to solve",\n  "problem_number": "integer - problem identifier (optional)",\n  "output_directory": "string - directory where solution and tests should be written (optional, defaults to \'problems\')"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failure",\n  "solution_file": "string - path to the written solution",\n  "test_file": "string - path to the test file",\n  "tests_passed": "boolean - whether all tests passed",\n  "tasks_completed": "array - list of completed tasks",\n  "message": "string - summary of the complete workflow",\n  "needs_clarification": "boolean - whether orchestrator needs more info",\n  "clarification_question": "string - question for user if needs_clarification is true"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- Problem description is too vague to break into tasks\n- Unclear what the expected behavior should be\n- Multiple valid interpretations exist\n- Tests fail repeatedly and can\'t determine why\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All tasks have been completed following TDD cycle\n- All tests pass for all tasks\n- Solution is complete and verified\n- User has been notified of any failures that couldn\'t be resolved\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.6%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.6\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'obje