{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:57:59", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-e7302640-90dc-4835-b6fb-46f5ba40e752', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "M2 Verification Tasks Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01B3QMEqFBmMQNsjCk2WDdUU', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01B3QMEqFBmMQNsjCk2WDdUU', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Vision**: Transform the Ensemble AI Executive Director from a simple coordinator into an intelligent planner with a Smart Task Decomposition Engine.\\n\\n**Objective**: Build a sophisticated task decomposition system that analyzes complex user requests, breaks them into optimal sub-tasks, generates dependency graphs, estimates resources, and creates efficient execution schedules.\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n**F1. Task Analysis & Decomposition**\\n- System must analyze task complexity and domain\\n- Break complex tasks into manageable sub-tasks\\n- Generate directed acyclic graphs (DAG) for task dependencies\\n- Support parallel execution planning\\n\\n**F2. Resource Management**\\n- Estimate required agents, tokens, cost, and time for each sub-task\\n- Optimize resource allocation using linear programming\\n- Generate execution schedules with parallel waves\\n- Support multiple agent types and specializations\\n\\n**F3. Learning & Improvement**\\n- Record actual vs. estimated performance data\\n- Continuously improve estimates based on historical data\\n- Track accuracy metrics over time\\n- Suggest optimization improvements\\n\\n**F4. API Integration**\\n- Provide REST endpoints for decomposition operations\\n- Support plan approval/rejection/modification workflows\\n- Integrate with existing FastAPI backend\\n- Maintain CORS compatibility\\n\\n**F5. User Interface**\\n- Visualize dependency graphs using Mermaid diagrams\\n- Display resource estimates and execution schedules\\n- Provide interactive plan approval interface\\n- Show agent assignments and timeline\\n\\n### Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n**N1. Performance**\\n- Decomposition analysis must complete within 5 seconds\\n- Support concurrent decomposition requests\\n- Maintain response time under 2 seconds for API calls\\n\\n**N2. Reliability**\\n- System must handle invalid inputs gracefully\\n- Provide meaningful error messages\\n- Maintain data integrity across operations\\n\\n**N3. Scalability**\\n- Support task graphs with up to 100 nodes\\n- Handle multiple concurrent users\\n- Efficient memory usage for large decompositions\\n\\n**N4. Maintainability**\\n- Test coverage > 80%\\n- Comprehensive documentation\\n- Clean, modular architecture\\n\\n## Technical Specifications\\n\\n### Technology Stack\\n- **Backend**: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic\\n- **Dependencies**: NetworkX (graph operations), PuLP (optimization)\\n- **Frontend**: React, Mermaid (diagram rendering)\\n- **Database**: SQLite (existing metrics.py integration)\\n- **Testing**: pytest\\n\\n### Data Models\\n\\n**TaskAnalysis**\\n- task_id: str\\n- complexity: str (simple|medium|complex)\\n- domain: str\\n- estimated_duration: float\\n- confidence_score: float\\n\\n**SubTask**\\n- sub_task_id: str\\n- description: str\\n- agent_type: str\\n- dependencies: List[str]\\n- estimated_resources: ResourceEstimate\\n\\n**DecompositionPlan**\\n- plan_id: str\\n- original_task: str\\n- sub_tasks: List[SubTask]\\n- dependency_graph: dict\\n- total_estimate: ResourceEstimate\\n- execution_schedule: Schedule\\n\\n### API Endpoints\\n\\n**POST /api/decompose**\\n- Input: user request text\\n- Output: DecompositionPlan JSON\\n- Functionality: Analyze and decompose task\\n\\n**POST /api/approve-plan**\\n- Input: plan_id, approval_status, modifications\\n- Output: execution status\\n- Functionality: Process plan approval/rejection\\n\\n**GET /api/decomposition-history**\\n- Input: optional filters\\n- Output: historical accuracy metrics\\n- Functionality: Retrieve learning data\\n\\n### File Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/agents/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_engine.py     # Core TaskDecompositionEngine\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_learner.py    # Learning and improvement module\\n\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/backend/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 main.py                     # Updated with new endpoints\\n\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx # React visualization component\\n\\ntests/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 test_decomposition.py       # Comprehensive test suite\\n\\ndocs/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md      # Architecture and usage docs\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n**Primary Success**\\n- Core engine can decompose complex tasks into valid DAGs\\n- Resource estimates are generated for all components\\n- Learning module improves estimate accuracy over time\\n- Frontend provides clear visualization and interaction\\n- All tests pass with >80% coverage\\n\\n**Quality Gates**\\n- No circular dependencies in generated graphs\\n- Resource estimates within 20% accuracy after learning\\n- API response times under 2 seconds\\n- UI components are responsive and accessible\\n- Complete documentation with examples\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n**Technical Assumptions**\\n- Existing Ensemble AI infrastructure is stable\\n- FastAPI backend can handle additional endpoints\\n- React frontend supports Mermaid diagram rendering\\n- NetworkX library provides adequate graph operations\\n\\n**Business Assumptions**\\n- Users will engage with decomposition plans before execution\\n- Historical data will improve estimate accuracy\\n- Linear programming approach is suitable for resource optimization\\n- DAG structure is appropriate for task dependencies\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n**Time Constraints**\\n- Implementation targeted for 6-10 hours of development work\\n- Must integrate with existing system without breaking changes\\n\\n**Technical Constraints**\\n- Must use existing database schema (metrics.py)\\n- Frontend must maintain current design patterns\\n- Backend must preserve existing API compatibility\\n\\n**Resource Constraints**\\n- Development limited to specified agent capabilities\\n- Must work within current infrastructure limits\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Real-time collaboration on decomposition plans\\n- Advanced machine learning for task prediction\\n- Integration with external project management tools\\n- Automated task execution (only planning)\\n- Multi-tenant support\\n\\n## Risk Analysis\\n\\n**High Risk**\\n- Graph complexity causing performance issues\\n- Learning algorithm convergence problems\\n\\n**Medium Risk**\\n- Frontend rendering large dependency graphs\\n- API integration compatibility issues\\n\\n**Low Risk**\\n- Data model changes\\n- Testing infrastructure setup\\n\\n## Implementation Methodology\\n\\n**Development Approach**: Test-Driven Development (TDD)\\n1. Write tests first for each component\\n2. Implement code to pass tests\\n3. Refactor for optimization\\n4. Integration testing between components\\n\\n**Quality Assurance**\\n- Unit tests for all core methods\\n- Integration tests for full workflows\\n- Performance benchmarking\\n- User acceptance testing for UI components"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016gKAz794HmGx98Roi37Fmr', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'M2 Verification Tasks Implementation', 'description': 'Implementing task decomposition verification engine for Ensemble AI'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016gKAz794HmGx98Roi37Fmr', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "6cec8c8c", "message": "Created project: M2 Verification Tasks Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "6cec8c8c", "project_name": "M2 Verification Tasks Implementation", "description": "Implementing task decomposition verification engine for Ensemble AI", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T01:57:48.696234", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T01:57:48.696234", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T01:57:48.696234", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'M2 Verification Tasks Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015S3Qg9umesXCWZziiW7Px6', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'project_name': 'M2 Verification Tasks Implementation'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015S3Qg9umesXCWZziiW7Px6', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'