{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:58:15", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-42773ad9-ef38-456b-936f-cce37391cea7', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/achievements_requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "achievements_system",\n  "project_id": "30aad396",\n  "task_id": "6bf1d826"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016WGKkiXQjgrbFMcQVwbAp2', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016WGKkiXQjgrbFMcQVwbAp2', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievements System - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** achievements_system  \\n**Project ID:** b7960dba  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nCreate a humorous Steam-style achievements system that awards different agent classes tongue-in-cheek achievements based on their actions. The system should track agent behavior and award achievements as milestones are reached, adding a playful gamification layer to the ensemble agent system.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Achievement Definition System**: Create a flexible schema for defining achievements with:\\n   - Achievement name (humorous/creative)\\n   - Description\\n   - Target agent class(es)\\n   - Trigger conditions\\n   - Icon/badge representation\\n   - Rarity tier (common, rare, epic, legendary)\\n\\n2. **Achievement Tracking**: Monitor agent actions and automatically award achievements when conditions are met\\n\\n3. **Achievement Display**: Present awarded achievements in the UI with visual feedback (toast notifications, achievement card displays)\\n\\n4. **Achievement History**: Maintain a persistent record of all achievements earned by agent class\\n\\n5. **Achievement Categories**: Organize achievements by theme:\\n   - Productivity (tasks completed, speed records)\\n   - Comedy (failures, quirky behaviors)\\n   - Milestones (first-time events)\\n   - Streaks (consecutive actions)\\n   - Meta (self-referential humor about being an AI)\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Backend Components:**\\n- Achievement data model and schema\\n- Achievement definition storage (JSON/database)\\n- Achievement tracking service that monitors agent activity\\n- Achievement award logic and evaluation engine\\n- API endpoints for:\\n  - Fetching available achievements\\n  - Fetching awarded achievements (by agent class, by project)\\n  - Triggering achievement evaluation\\n  - Achievement statistics\\n\\n**Frontend Components:**\\n- Achievement notification system (toast/banner when earned)\\n- Achievement gallery/showcase view\\n- Achievement progress indicators (for multi-step achievements)\\n- Agent profile page showing earned achievements\\n- Achievement filtering and sorting\\n\\n**Achievement Content:**\\n- 20-30 humorous achievements per major agent class:\\n  - Executive Director\\n  - Development Manager\\n  - System Architect\\n  - Code Writer\\n  - Code Tester\\n  - Bug Fixer\\n  - Documentation Writer\\n- Examples:\\n  - \\"Executive Overreach\\" - Executive Director tries to write code (blocked by permissions)\\n  - \\"Infinite Recursion Champion\\" - Spawned 10 sub-agents in a single task\\n  - \\"Test Whisperer\\" - Code Tester achieves 100% test coverage\\n  - \\"Bug Whisperer\\" - Bug Fixer fixes 50 bugs without creating new ones\\n  - \\"RTFM Generator\\" - Documentation Writer creates docs longer than the code\\n  - \\"Premature Optimization\\" - Code Writer refactors before requirements are clear\\n  - \\"Merge Conflict Survivor\\" - Successfully resolved 10 Git conflicts\\n  - \\"Commit Message Poet\\" - 10 commit messages >100 characters\\n  - \\"TDD Purist\\" - Wrote tests before code 100 times\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- User-created custom achievements (Phase 2 feature)\\n- Achievement leaderboards across different ensemble instances\\n- Achievement trading or social features\\n- Blockchain/NFT integration for achievements\\n- Achievements that affect agent behavior or permissions\\n- Multiplayer/competitive achievement mechanics\\n- External platform integration (actual Steam, Discord badges, etc.)\\n\\n## User Personas\\n\\n**Primary User: Developer/Operator**\\n- Monitors ensemble agent activity\\n- Enjoys gamification and humor in development tools\\n- Appreciates insights into agent behavior patterns\\n- Values both functionality and entertainment\\n\\n**Secondary User: Executive Director (Self-Aware AI)**\\n- Tracks performance metrics indirectly through achievements\\n- Gains insight into which agents are most active\\n- Uses achievement patterns to identify optimization opportunities\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n### F1: Achievement Definition System\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** JSON-based achievement schema with:\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\"id\\": \\"executive_overreach\\",\\n    \\"name\\": \\"Executive Overreach\\",\\n    \\"description\\": \\"Attempted to write code despite lacking can_write_code permission\\",\\n    \\"agent_class\\": \\"executive_director\\",\\n    \\"category\\": \\"comedy\\",\\n    \\"rarity\\": \\"common\\",\\n    \\"trigger\\": {\\n      \\"event_type\\": \\"permission_denied\\",\\n      \\"action\\": \\"write_code_file\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"icon\\": \\"\\ud83d\\udeab\\ud83d\\udcbb\\",\\n    \\"points\\": 10\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n### F2: Real-Time Achievement Tracking\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** Service that monitors agent activity logs and evaluates achievement conditions\\n- Integrates with existing activity tracker\\n- Triggers award ceremony when conditions met\\n\\n### F3: Achievement Notification UI\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** Toast notification appears when achievement earned\\n- Shows achievement name, description, icon, rarity\\n- Plays subtle animation/sound effect\\n- Links to full achievement details\\n\\n### F4: Achievement Gallery\\n- **Priority:** Medium\\n- **Description:** Dedicated page showing:\\n  - All available achievements (locked/unlocked state)\\n  - Filter by agent class, category, rarity\\n  - Progress bars for multi-step achievements\\n  - Statistics (total earned, completion percentage)\\n\\n### F5: Agent Profile Achievements\\n- **Priority:** Medium\\n- **Description:** Each agent class profile shows:\\n  - Recently earned achievements\\n  - Rarest achievements\\n  - Achievement count and total points\\n  - Links to full gallery filtered by that agent\\n\\n### F6: Achievement Persistence\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** Store achievement awards in database/JSON file\\n- Persist across sessions\\n- Track timestamps of when achieved\\n- Support for achievement history/timeline\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Integration:** Must integrate with existing:\\n   - Activity tracking system (`activity_tracker.py`)\\n   - Agent spawn/execution pipeline\\n   - Project tracking system\\n   - Frontend React components\\n\\n2. **Performance:** Achievement evaluation should not slow down agent execution\\n   - Async/background processing\\n   - Batch evaluation where possible\\n\\n3. **Storage:** Use existing storage patterns:\\n   - JSON files in `~/.ensemble/achievements/`\\n   - Or extend existing SQLite/database if present\\n\\n4. **Technology Stack:**\\n   - Backend: Python/FastAPI (existing)\\n   - Frontend: React + TypeScript (existing)\\n   - Storage: JSON or SQLite\\n   - Real-time updates: WebSocket or polling\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional:**\\n   - \\u2705 20+ achievements defined per major agent class\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements automatically awarded when conditions met\\n   - \\u2705 Notifications appear within 2 seconds of earning\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement history persists across sessions\\n   - \\u2705 Gallery displays all achievements with correct locked/unlocked state\\n\\n2. **User Experience:**\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements are genuinely funny/entertaining\\n   - \\u2705 Notifications are non-intrusive but noticeable\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement progress is clear and motivating\\n   - \\u2705 UI integrates seamlessly with existing interface\\n\\n3. **Technical:**\\n   - \\u2705 No performance degradation in agent execution\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement data persists reliably\\n   - \\u2705 Code follows existing project patterns\\n   - \\u2705 Unit tests cover achievement logic (>80% coverage)\\n   - \\u2705 Integration tests verify end-to-end flow\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Humor Tone:** Achievements should be lighthearted and self-aware, poking fun at AI/developer culture without being mean-spirited\\n\\n2. **Privacy:** Achievement data is local to the ensemble instance (no external reporting)\\n\\n3. **Extensibility:** System should be designed for easy addition of new achievements in the future\\n\\n4. **Performance:** Existing activity tracking provides sufficient event data for achievement triggers\\n\\n5. **UI Framework:** React frontend exists with component library/patterns to follow\\n\\n6. **Backend API:** FastAPI backend exists with established patterns for new endpoints\\n\\n7. **User Preferences:** Users can disable achievement notifications if desired (settings toggle)\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n1. **Maintainability:** Achievement definitions should be easy to add/modify without code changes\\n2. **Testability:** Achievement trigger logic should be unit-testable in isolation\\n3. **Scalability:** System should handle 100+ achievements without performance issues\\n4. **Accessibility:** Achievement UI should be screen-reader friendly\\n5. **Localization:** Initial English-only, but structure should support i18n in future\\n\\n## Risks & Mitigations\\n\\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\\n|------|--------|------------|\\n| Achievement evaluation slows agent execution | High | Use async background processing, batch evaluation |\\n| Activity tracker doesn\'t capture needed events | Medium | Extend activity tracker to emit additional events |\\n| Notification fatigue (too many achievements) | Medium | Implement cooldown periods, configurable frequency |\\n| Achievement definitions become stale/outdated | Low | Regular review process, community suggestions |\\n| Storage conflicts with existing data | Medium | Use isolated namespace/directory for achievements |\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n1. **M1: Requirements & Architecture** (Current)\\n   - Requirements document complete\\n   - Architecture design approved\\n   - Achievement content brainstormed\\n\\n2. **M2: Backend Implementation**\\n   - Achievement data model\\n   - Tracking service\\n   - API endpoints\\n   - Integration with activity tracker\\n\\n3. **M3: Frontend Implementation**\\n   - Notification component\\n   - Achievement gallery\\n   - Agent profile integration\\n   - Settings/preferences\\n\\n4. **M4: Content & Testing**\\n   - All achievement definitions created\\n   - Unit tests (>80% coverage)\\n   - Integration tests\\n   - Manual QA\\n\\n5. **M5: Deployment & Documentation**\\n   - User documentation\\n   - Developer documentation (adding new achievements)\\n   - Deployment to production\\n   - Launch celebration achievement \\ud83c\\udf89\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\nNone - proceeding with assumptions documented above. Executive Director has made decisive choices for:\\n- Technology stack (existing Python/React)\\n- Storage approach (JSON files in ~/.ensemble/achievements/)\\n- Achievement count (20-30 per agent class)\\n- Notification mechanism (toast notifications)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Architecture Phase  \\n**Next Step:** Spawn Development Manager with this requirements document\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01U7G5gj3mdVWY5aHBckQBey', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'update_task', 'project_id': '30aad396', 'task_id': '6bf1d826', 'status': 'in_progress', 'note': 'Starting Development Manager workflow - analyzing requirements and planning milestones'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01U7G5gj3mdVWY5aHBckQBey', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Updated task status to in_progress"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EB5J9cTncDQxJpo4DatpZk', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Achievements System - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project Name:** achievements_system  \n**Development Manager:** Orchestrating implementation from requirements through delivery  \n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Foundation & Backend Core\n**Duration:** 3-4 days  \n**Priority:** Critical Path  \n\n**Objective:**  \nEstablish the foundational backend architecture and core achievement tracking system.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Achievement data model and schema\n- Achievement tracking service with activity integration\n- Basic API endpoints for achievement management\n- Achievement definition storage system (JSON-based)\n- Core achievement evaluation engine\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ Achievement schema supports all required fields (name, description, agent_class, category, rarity, trigger conditions)\n- ✅ Tracking service successfully monitors agent activity and evaluates trigger conditions\n- ✅ API endpoints allow fetching and awarding achievements\n- ✅ Achievement data persists across sessions in `~/.ensemble/achievements/`\n- ✅ No performance impact on existing agent execution (async processing)\n- ✅ Unit tests achieve >80% coverage for core logic\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- None (foundational milestone)\n\n**Key Technical Decisions:**\n- JSON file storage in `~/.ensemble/achievements/` directory\n- Async background processing for achievement evaluation\n- Integration with existing activity_tracker.py\n- FastAPI endpoints following existing patterns\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 2: Frontend Achievement System\n**Duration:** 2-3 days  \n**Priority:** High  \n\n**Objective:**  \nImplement user-facing achievement features including notifications, gallery, and agent profile integration.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Achievement notification component (toast-style)\n- Achievement gallery with filtering and sorting\n- Agent profile achievement display\n- Achievement progress indicators\n- Settings for notification preferences\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ Toast notifications appear within 2 seconds of earning achievements\n- ✅ Gallery displays all achievements with correct locked/unlocked state\n- ✅ Filtering works by agent class, category, and rarity\n- ✅ Agent profiles show recently earned and rarest achievements\n- ✅ Progress bars display correctly for multi-step achievements\n- ✅ Users can disable notifications via settings\n- ✅ UI integrates seamlessly with existing React components\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Milestone 1 (Backend Core) must be complete\n- Existing React frontend and component library\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 3: Achievement Content & Integration\n**Duration:** 2-3 days  \n**Priority:** Medium  \n\n**Objective:**  \nCreate comprehensive achievement definitions and ensure full integration with agent behaviors.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- 20-30 humorous achievements per major agent class (140+ total)\n- Achievement categories (productivity, comedy, milestones, streaks, meta)\n- Complete integration with all agent spawn/execution paths\n- Achievement icon system\n- Rarity balancing and point systems\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ All major agent classes have 20+ unique achievements\n- ✅ Achievements are genuinely funny and self-aware\n- ✅ Achievement triggers capture key agent behaviors accurately\n- ✅ Rarity distribution is balanced (common: 60%, rare: 25%, epic: 12%, legendary: 3%)\n- ✅ Icons/emojis are appropriate and visually distinct\n- ✅ All agent execution paths can trigger appropriate achievements\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Milestone 1 (Backend Core) complete\n- Milestone 2 (Frontend) substantially complete for testing\n\n**Example Achievements per Agent Class:**\n- **Executive Director:** "Executive Overreach", "Infinite Recursion Champion", "Delegation Master"\n- **Development Manager:** "Milestone Mania", "Scope Creep Survivor", "Architecture Whisperer"\n- **System Architect:** "Over-Engineering Champion", "Pattern Enthusiast", "Abstraction Layer Lord"\n- **Code Writer:** "Premature Optimization", "Variable Namer Extraordinaire", "Regex Wizard"\n- **Code Tester:** "Test Whisperer", "100% Coverage Zealot", "Edge Case Explorer"\n- **Bug Fixer:** "Bug Whisperer", "Regression Prevention Pro", "Stack Trace Detective"\n- **Documentation Writer:** "RTFM Generator", "Commit Message Poet", "Documentation Completionist"\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 4: Testing & Quality Assurance\n**Duration:** 2 days  \n**Priority:** High  \n\n**Objective:**  \nComprehensive testing and quality assurance to ensure system reliability and user experience.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Complete unit test suite (>80% coverage)\n- Integration tests for end-to-end achievement flow\n- Performance testing (no degradation in agent execution)\n- User experience testing and refinement\n- Bug fixes and optimizations\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ Unit tests cover all achievement logic with >80% coverage\n- ✅ Integration tests verify achievement earning from agent actions\n- ✅ Performance tests show no measurable impact on agent execution times\n- ✅ Manual testing confirms all UI components work correctly\n- ✅ Achievement notifications are non-intrusive but noticeable\n- ✅ All defined achievements can be earned through normal agent usage\n- ✅ Data persistence is reliable across application restarts\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- All previous milestones substantially complete\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 5: Documentation & Deployment\n**Duration:** 1-2 days  \n**Priority:** Medium  \n\n**Objective:**  \nComplete project documentation and prepare for production deployment.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- User documentation (how to view/manage achievements)\n- Developer documentation (how to add new achievements)\n- API documentation\n- Deployment guide and configuration\n- Launch celebration and monitoring setup\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ User documentation explains all achievement features clearly\n- ✅ Developer docs provide step-by-step guide for adding achievements\n- ✅ API endpoints are fully documented\n- ✅ Deployment process is documented and tested\n- ✅ System monitoring confirms achievements work in production\n- ✅ Special "Launch Day" achievement is available and earned\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- All previous milestones complete and tested\n\n---\n\n## Risk Management\n\n**High Risk Items:**\n1. **Performance Impact** - Achievement evaluation must not slow agent execution\n   - *Mitigation:* Async processing, batch evaluation, performance testing in M4\n\n2. **Integration Complexity** - Integrating with existing activity tracker and agent pipeline\n   - *Mitigation:* Early integration in M1, incremental testing\n\n**Medium Risk Items:**\n1. **Achievement Trigger Accuracy** - Ensuring achievements trigger at correct times\n   - *Mitigation:* Thorough testing in M3/M4, iterative refinement\n\n2. **UI/UX Integration** - Seamless integration with existing frontend\n   - *Mitigation:* Follow existing patterns, early UI prototyping in M2\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n**Functional Success:**\n- All 140+ achievements implemented and testable\n- Achievement earning works reliably across all agent classes\n- No performance degradation in agent execution\n- Achievement data persists correctly\n\n**User Experience Success:**\n- Achievements are entertaining and motivating\n- Notifications are appropriately timed and non-intrusive\n- Gallery and profile views are intuitive and useful\n- System feels like a natural part of the ensemble interface\n\n**Technical Success:**\n- >80% test coverage maintained\n- Code follows existing project patterns and standards\n- System is extensible for future achievement additions\n- Documentation enables maintenance and extension\n\n---\n\n**Status:** Planning Complete - Ready for Architecture Phase  \n**Next Steps:** \n1. Spawn System Architect for architecture design\n2. Begin Milestone 1 implementation with backend focus\n3. Maintain sequential execution through all milestones'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EB5J9cTncDQxJpo4DatpZk', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_015812.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_015812.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012AYsZfqvJJCAzY4hUYWyYd', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/achievements_requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'achievements_system'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012AYsZfqvJJCAzY4hUYWyYd', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
