{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:58:20", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-408bd1b4-1f12-4eeb-ae30-af49c082b11d', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Decomposition Milestones Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01A92VTvoGBHfRPrvkk24X28', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01A92VTvoGBHfRPrvkk24X28', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Vision**: Transform the Ensemble AI Executive Director from a simple coordinator into an intelligent planner with a Smart Task Decomposition Engine.\\n\\n**Objective**: Build a sophisticated task decomposition system that analyzes complex user requests, breaks them into optimal sub-tasks, generates dependency graphs, estimates resources, and creates efficient execution schedules.\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n**F1. Task Analysis & Decomposition**\\n- System must analyze task complexity and domain\\n- Break complex tasks into manageable sub-tasks\\n- Generate directed acyclic graphs (DAG) for task dependencies\\n- Support parallel execution planning\\n\\n**F2. Resource Management**\\n- Estimate required agents, tokens, cost, and time for each sub-task\\n- Optimize resource allocation using linear programming\\n- Generate execution schedules with parallel waves\\n- Support multiple agent types and specializations\\n\\n**F3. Learning & Improvement**\\n- Record actual vs. estimated performance data\\n- Continuously improve estimates based on historical data\\n- Track accuracy metrics over time\\n- Suggest optimization improvements\\n\\n**F4. API Integration**\\n- Provide REST endpoints for decomposition operations\\n- Support plan approval/rejection/modification workflows\\n- Integrate with existing FastAPI backend\\n- Maintain CORS compatibility\\n\\n**F5. User Interface**\\n- Visualize dependency graphs using Mermaid diagrams\\n- Display resource estimates and execution schedules\\n- Provide interactive plan approval interface\\n- Show agent assignments and timeline\\n\\n### Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n**N1. Performance**\\n- Decomposition analysis must complete within 5 seconds\\n- Support concurrent decomposition requests\\n- Maintain response time under 2 seconds for API calls\\n\\n**N2. Reliability**\\n- System must handle invalid inputs gracefully\\n- Provide meaningful error messages\\n- Maintain data integrity across operations\\n\\n**N3. Scalability**\\n- Support task graphs with up to 100 nodes\\n- Handle multiple concurrent users\\n- Efficient memory usage for large decompositions\\n\\n**N4. Maintainability**\\n- Test coverage > 80%\\n- Comprehensive documentation\\n- Clean, modular architecture\\n\\n## Technical Specifications\\n\\n### Technology Stack\\n- **Backend**: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic\\n- **Dependencies**: NetworkX (graph operations), PuLP (optimization)\\n- **Frontend**: React, Mermaid (diagram rendering)\\n- **Database**: SQLite (existing metrics.py integration)\\n- **Testing**: pytest\\n\\n### Data Models\\n\\n**TaskAnalysis**\\n- task_id: str\\n- complexity: str (simple|medium|complex)\\n- domain: str\\n- estimated_duration: float\\n- confidence_score: float\\n\\n**SubTask**\\n- sub_task_id: str\\n- description: str\\n- agent_type: str\\n- dependencies: List[str]\\n- estimated_resources: ResourceEstimate\\n\\n**DecompositionPlan**\\n- plan_id: str\\n- original_task: str\\n- sub_tasks: List[SubTask]\\n- dependency_graph: dict\\n- total_estimate: ResourceEstimate\\n- execution_schedule: Schedule\\n\\n### API Endpoints\\n\\n**POST /api/decompose**\\n- Input: user request text\\n- Output: DecompositionPlan JSON\\n- Functionality: Analyze and decompose task\\n\\n**POST /api/approve-plan**\\n- Input: plan_id, approval_status, modifications\\n- Output: execution status\\n- Functionality: Process plan approval/rejection\\n\\n**GET /api/decomposition-history**\\n- Input: optional filters\\n- Output: historical accuracy metrics\\n- Functionality: Retrieve learning data\\n\\n### File Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/agents/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_engine.py     # Core TaskDecompositionEngine\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_learner.py    # Learning and improvement module\\n\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/backend/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 main.py                     # Updated with new endpoints\\n\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx # React visualization component\\n\\ntests/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 test_decomposition.py       # Comprehensive test suite\\n\\ndocs/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md      # Architecture and usage docs\\n```\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n**Primary Success**\\n- Core engine can decompose complex tasks into valid DAGs\\n- Resource estimates are generated for all components\\n- Learning module improves estimate accuracy over time\\n- Frontend provides clear visualization and interaction\\n- All tests pass with >80% coverage\\n\\n**Quality Gates**\\n- No circular dependencies in generated graphs\\n- Resource estimates within 20% accuracy after learning\\n- API response times under 2 seconds\\n- UI components are responsive and accessible\\n- Complete documentation with examples\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n**Technical Assumptions**\\n- Existing Ensemble AI infrastructure is stable\\n- FastAPI backend can handle additional endpoints\\n- React frontend supports Mermaid diagram rendering\\n- NetworkX library provides adequate graph operations\\n\\n**Business Assumptions**\\n- Users will engage with decomposition plans before execution\\n- Historical data will improve estimate accuracy\\n- Linear programming approach is suitable for resource optimization\\n- DAG structure is appropriate for task dependencies\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n**Time Constraints**\\n- Implementation targeted for 6-10 hours of development work\\n- Must integrate with existing system without breaking changes\\n\\n**Technical Constraints**\\n- Must use existing database schema (metrics.py)\\n- Frontend must maintain current design patterns\\n- Backend must preserve existing API compatibility\\n\\n**Resource Constraints**\\n- Development limited to specified agent capabilities\\n- Must work within current infrastructure limits\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Real-time collaboration on decomposition plans\\n- Advanced machine learning for task prediction\\n- Integration with external project management tools\\n- Automated task execution (only planning)\\n- Multi-tenant support\\n\\n## Risk Analysis\\n\\n**High Risk**\\n- Graph complexity causing performance issues\\n- Learning algorithm convergence problems\\n\\n**Medium Risk**\\n- Frontend rendering large dependency graphs\\n- API integration compatibility issues\\n\\n**Low Risk**\\n- Data model changes\\n- Testing infrastructure setup\\n\\n## Implementation Methodology\\n\\n**Development Approach**: Test-Driven Development (TDD)\\n1. Write tests first for each component\\n2. Implement code to pass tests\\n3. Refactor for optimization\\n4. Integration testing between components\\n\\n**Quality Assurance**\\n- Unit tests for all core methods\\n- Integration tests for full workflows\\n- Performance benchmarking\\n- User acceptance testing for UI components"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011GfuBQv1zBHofvqmae94L6', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Milestone Plan\n\n## Milestone 1: Core Engine & Backend Development\n### Objectives\n- Implement TaskDecompositionEngine core logic\n- Design initial data models\n- Create initial API endpoints\n- Set up basic learning infrastructure\n\n### Deliverables\n- `decomposition_engine.py` with task analysis functions\n- Data model implementations\n- FastAPI endpoint stubs\n- Basic resource estimation logic\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Core decomposition algorithm works for simple tasks\n- Can generate basic dependency graphs\n- Endpoints return valid JSON responses\n- Basic unit tests pass\n\n## Milestone 2: Advanced Decomposition & Learning\n### Objectives\n- Enhance task complexity handling\n- Implement learning module\n- Improve resource estimation\n- Add historical tracking\n\n### Deliverables\n- Advanced decomposition strategies\n- Learning algorithm implementation\n- Enhanced resource estimation\n- Historical performance tracking\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Handle medium to complex task domains\n- Learning module shows improvement over iterations\n- Resource estimates within 30% accuracy\n- Comprehensive integration tests\n\n## Milestone 3: Frontend Integration & Visualization\n### Objectives\n- Create React visualization component\n- Implement interactive plan approval\n- Design dependency graph rendering\n- Complete user interface\n\n### Deliverables\n- `TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx`\n- Interactive plan management UI\n- Mermaid diagram integration\n- Full frontend-backend connectivity\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Visualize task dependency graphs\n- Interactive plan approval workflow\n- Responsive and accessible UI\n- Performance under 2-second response time\n\n## Milestone 4: Final Testing & Documentation\n### Objectives\n- Comprehensive test coverage\n- Performance optimization\n- Complete documentation\n- Final system validation\n\n### Deliverables\n- Full test suite\n- Performance benchmarks\n- Detailed documentation\n- Final system validation report\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- >80% test coverage\n- All performance requirements met\n- Comprehensive usage documentation\n- No critical bugs identified'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011GfuBQv1zBHofvqmae94L6', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_015803.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_015803.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- A