{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:58:25", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c670190c-be26-4e2d-84d6-b7330ac320b4', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/mobile_responsive_requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Mobile Responsive UI and Agent Recovery",\n  "project_id": "52d83b03",\n  "task_id": "5dd99efe"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015qTC3Z67YigmXw5ApTvzjS', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/mobile_responsive_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015qTC3Z67YigmXw5ApTvzjS', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Mobile Responsive UI Enhancement Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Vision**: Make the Ensemble AI web UI responsive and usable on mobile devices while addressing system stability issues with stalled agents.\\n\\n**Background**: The current Ensemble UI is built with React and Bootstrap, but lacks proper mobile responsiveness. The three-column layout doesn\'t adapt well to smaller screens. Additionally, the system has several agents that have failed with BadRequestError, suggesting configuration or API issues that need resolution.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Objectives\\n1. **Mobile Responsiveness**: Make the UI fully responsive and usable on mobile devices (320px-768px width)\\n2. **Agent Recovery**: Resume/fix high priority stalled agents that have failed with BadRequestError\\n3. **Improved UX**: Ensure all features are accessible and usable on touch devices\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n1. UI renders correctly on mobile devices (320px-768px viewport)\\n2. All interactive elements are touch-friendly (minimum 44x44px tap targets)\\n3. Navigation works seamlessly on mobile\\n4. Failed agents are identified and issues resolved\\n5. System can successfully spawn and run agents without BadRequestError\\n6. All existing functionality remains working on desktop\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n#### 1. Mobile UI Enhancements\\n- **Responsive Layout**: Convert 3-column layout to stack vertically on mobile\\n- **Navigation**: Add mobile-friendly navigation (hamburger menu or tab system)\\n- **Touch Optimization**: Ensure buttons, controls, and interactive elements are touch-friendly\\n- **Viewport Configuration**: Add proper meta tags for mobile rendering\\n- **Typography**: Adjust font sizes for readability on small screens\\n- **Collapsible Sections**: Ensure all collapsible sections work well on mobile\\n- **Form Inputs**: Optimize form controls for mobile (larger touch targets, appropriate keyboard types)\\n\\n#### 2. Agent System Recovery\\n- **Error Analysis**: Identify root cause of BadRequestError failures\\n- **Configuration Fix**: Correct API configuration issues (model names, API keys, parameters)\\n- **Agent Resume**: Implement mechanism to resume or restart failed agents\\n- **Priority Agents**: Focus on high-priority agents first:\\n  - leadership/development_manager\\n  - testers/unit_test_lead\\n  - executive_director instances\\n\\n#### 3. Responsive Breakpoints\\n- **Mobile**: 320px-767px (single column, stacked layout)\\n- **Tablet**: 768px-1023px (two column or adaptive layout)\\n- **Desktop**: 1024px+ (current three-column layout)\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign or rebranding\\n- Adding new features beyond responsiveness\\n- Backend API changes (unless required for agent recovery)\\n- Performance optimization beyond responsive design\\n- Accessibility audit (though basic accessibility will be maintained)\\n- Progressive Web App (PWA) features\\n- Offline functionality\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n### Technical Constraints\\n1. Must maintain existing React + Bootstrap architecture\\n2. Must not break existing desktop functionality\\n3. Should use CSS media queries and Bootstrap responsive utilities\\n4. Must work in modern mobile browsers (Safari iOS 14+, Chrome Android 90+)\\n\\n### Resource Constraints\\n1. Changes should be minimal and focused on responsiveness\\n2. Avoid major architectural changes\\n3. Use existing Bootstrap grid system and utilities\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n#### FR1: Mobile Layout Adaptation\\n- **FR1.1**: On screens < 768px, convert 3-column layout to single-column stacked layout\\n- **FR1.2**: Sections should stack in order: Input Form \\u2192 Questions \\u2192 Activity Feed \\u2192 Agent Tasks \\u2192 Files \\u2192 Hierarchy\\n- **FR1.3**: All sections should be independently scrollable or use native page scrolling\\n\\n#### FR2: Mobile Navigation\\n- **FR2.1**: Add tab navigation or collapsible sections for main content areas\\n- **FR2.2**: Header should remain fixed or easily accessible on mobile\\n- **FR2.3**: Poll interval controls should be accessible but not take excessive space\\n\\n#### FR3: Touch-Friendly Controls\\n- **FR3.1**: All buttons and interactive elements must be minimum 44x44px\\n- **FR3.2**: Form inputs should have appropriate spacing (padding) for touch\\n- **FR3.3**: Dropdown selects should be mobile-friendly\\n- **FR3.4**: Badge and status indicators should remain readable\\n\\n#### FR4: Responsive Typography\\n- **FR4.1**: Font sizes should scale appropriately for mobile (14px-16px body text)\\n- **FR4.2**: Headers should be proportionally sized\\n- **FR4.3**: Code blocks and file content should be readable with horizontal scroll if needed\\n\\n#### FR5: Agent Recovery System\\n- **FR5.1**: Identify all agents with BadRequestError\\n- **FR5.2**: Analyze error logs to determine root cause (likely model name or API configuration)\\n- **FR5.3**: Fix configuration issues in agent spawning code or API calls\\n- **FR5.4**: Provide mechanism to retry failed agents or restart from checkpoint\\n\\n### Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n#### NFR1: Performance\\n- Mobile responsiveness should not impact load time\\n- CSS media queries should use efficient selectors\\n- No significant increase in bundle size\\n\\n#### NFR2: Compatibility\\n- Must work on iOS Safari 14+\\n- Must work on Chrome Android 90+\\n- Must work on Firefox Mobile\\n- Maintain backward compatibility with desktop browsers\\n\\n#### NFR3: Maintainability\\n- Use Bootstrap\'s built-in responsive utilities where possible\\n- Keep custom CSS organized and documented\\n- Follow existing code style and conventions\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Mobile viewport meta tag** is missing and needs to be added to index.html\\n2. **BadRequestError** is likely caused by incorrect model names or API configuration\\n3. Users will primarily use portrait orientation on mobile devices\\n4. The backend API endpoints are already responsive and work on mobile\\n5. No authentication or authorization changes are needed\\n6. The agent system has the capability to resume/retry failed tasks\\n\\n## Risks & Mitigation\\n\\n| Risk | Impact | Probability | Mitigation |\\n|------|--------|-------------|------------|\\n| Bootstrap grid doesn\'t adapt well | High | Low | Use custom CSS media queries if needed |\\n| Touch targets too small | Medium | Medium | Test on real devices, increase button sizes |\\n| Agent errors require backend changes | High | Medium | Document findings, coordinate with backend if needed |\\n| Layout breaks on specific devices | Medium | Low | Test on multiple devices/emulators |\\n| Performance degradation on mobile | Low | Low | Profile and optimize if issues arise |\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n### Phase 1: Mobile UI Implementation\\n1. Add viewport meta tag to HTML\\n2. Implement responsive breakpoints using Bootstrap grid\\n3. Convert 3-column to stacked layout on mobile\\n4. Adjust typography and spacing for mobile\\n5. Ensure touch-friendly controls\\n6. Test on multiple device sizes\\n\\n### Phase 2: Agent System Analysis & Recovery\\n1. Query metrics database for failed agents\\n2. Analyze error messages and logs\\n3. Identify root cause (model config, API keys, parameters)\\n4. Implement fixes in agent spawning/configuration\\n5. Test agent spawning with corrected configuration\\n6. Resume high-priority failed agents\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing & Validation\\n1. Test on real mobile devices (iOS, Android)\\n2. Verify all functionality works on mobile\\n3. Ensure desktop functionality unchanged\\n4. Validate agent recovery successful\\n5. Document changes and any configuration updates\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Updated Frontend Code**:\\n   - Modified App.jsx with responsive layout\\n   - Updated component files for mobile optimization\\n   - Custom CSS for responsive design (if needed)\\n   - Updated index.html with viewport meta tag\\n\\n2. **Agent Recovery Documentation**:\\n   - Error analysis report\\n   - Root cause identification\\n   - Configuration fixes applied\\n   - Resume/restart procedures\\n\\n3. **Testing Documentation**:\\n   - Mobile device testing results\\n   - Screenshots of responsive layout\\n   - Agent recovery test results\\n\\n4. **Updated README**: Documentation of mobile support and any configuration changes\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- Existing Ensemble UI codebase\\n- Bootstrap 5.x responsive utilities\\n- React 18.x\\n- Backend API (for agent recovery)\\n- Access to ~/.ensemble/metrics.db for agent analysis\\n\\n## Technology Stack\\n\\n- **Frontend**: React 18.x, Bootstrap 5.x\\n- **Styling**: Bootstrap responsive utilities, custom CSS media queries\\n- **Build**: Vite\\n- **Testing**: Manual testing on mobile devices/emulators\\n- **Agent System**: Python-based agent orchestration system\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- The user request mentions \\"resume high priority stalled agents\\" - this suggests there are agents that are currently blocked/failed\\n- Database query shows multiple agents failed with BadRequestError, most recently development_manager and unit_test_lead\\n- This is likely a configuration issue (wrong model names, API parameters) rather than a code logic issue\\n- The mobile responsiveness work is straightforward, but agent recovery may require investigation into the agent spawning system\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NFZzQRmWqacAJ6zKqfd8D5', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Mobile Responsive UI and Agent Recovery', 'description': 'Make the Ensemble AI web UI responsive and usable on mobile devices while addressing system stability issues with stalled agents'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NFZzQRmWqacAJ6zKqfd8D5', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "d596f938", "message": "Created project: Mobile Responsive UI and Agent Recovery", "summary": {"project_id": "d596f938", "project_name": "Mobile Responsive UI and Agent Recovery", "description": "Make the Ensemble AI web UI responsive and usable on mobile devices while addressing system stability issues with stalled agents", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T01:57:48.479721", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T01:57:48.479721", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T01:57:48.479721", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Mobile Responsive UI and Agent Recovery\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011HSAueGJFQvexZEtAyTDMc', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': "# Mobile Responsive UI and Agent Recovery - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project**: Mobile Responsive UI and Agent Recovery  \n**Objectives**: Make the Ensemble AI web UI fully responsive for mobile devices and resolve system stability issues with stalled agents  \n**Duration**: 3 Milestones (estimated 3-4 development cycles)\n\n## Milestone 1: Mobile UI Foundation & Responsive Layout\n**Duration**: 1-2 development cycles  \n**Priority**: High  \n\n### Objective\nEstablish the foundational responsive design structure and convert the three-column desktop layout to a mobile-friendly single-column stacked layout.\n\n### Deliverables\n- Add viewport meta tag to HTML head for proper mobile rendering\n- Implement responsive breakpoints (mobile: 320-767px, tablet: 768-1023px, desktop: 1024px+)\n- Convert 3-column layout to stacked single-column layout on mobile\n- Ensure proper section ordering on mobile: Input Form → Questions → Activity Feed → Agent Tasks → Files → Hierarchy\n- Implement responsive typography (14px-16px body text on mobile)\n- Basic touch-friendly control sizing (minimum 44x44px tap targets)\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ UI renders correctly on mobile viewport (320px-768px)\n- ✅ All sections stack vertically in proper order on mobile\n- ✅ Text is readable without horizontal scrolling\n- ✅ Basic touch targets meet minimum 44x44px requirement\n- ✅ Desktop functionality remains unchanged\n- ✅ Layout works in mobile Safari iOS 14+ and Chrome Android 90+\n\n### Dependencies\n- Existing React + Bootstrap codebase\n- Access to frontend source files\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: Mobile UX Optimization & Navigation\n**Duration**: 1-2 development cycles  \n**Priority**: High  \n\n### Objective\nEnhance the mobile user experience with optimized navigation, touch-friendly controls, and improved mobile-specific interactions.\n\n### Deliverables\n- Implement mobile navigation system (tabs or collapsible sections)\n- Optimize all form controls for touch interaction\n- Add proper spacing and padding for mobile controls\n- Implement collapsible sections for better mobile content organization\n- Optimize dropdown selects and other form elements for mobile\n- Ensure header accessibility on mobile (fixed or easily reachable)\n- Implement horizontal scroll for code blocks and wide content\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ Navigation is intuitive and efficient on mobile\n- ✅ All buttons and controls are easily tappable (44x44px minimum)\n- ✅ Form inputs work smoothly on mobile keyboards\n- ✅ Content sections can be easily navigated on mobile\n- ✅ Code blocks and wide content are accessible with proper scrolling\n- ✅ Poll interval controls are accessible but space-efficient\n\n### Dependencies\n- Completion of Milestone 1\n- Mobile testing devices or emulators\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 3: Agent System Recovery & Testing\n**Duration**: 1-2 development cycles  \n**Priority**: Critical  \n\n### Objective\nAnalyze and resolve BadRequestError issues affecting agent system stability, implement recovery mechanisms, and comprehensive testing of both mobile UI and agent functionality.\n\n### Deliverables\n- Error analysis report identifying root cause of BadRequestError failures\n- Configuration fixes for agent spawning (model names, API parameters, API keys)\n- Implementation of agent recovery/retry mechanisms\n- Resume high-priority failed agents (development_manager, unit_test_lead, executive_director)\n- Comprehensive mobile testing across devices\n- Updated documentation for mobile support and agent configuration\n- Performance validation ensuring no degradation\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ Root cause of BadRequestError identified and documented\n- ✅ Agent configuration issues resolved\n- ✅ Failed agents successfully resume/restart\n- ✅ New agents spawn without BadRequestError\n- ✅ Mobile UI tested on real devices (iOS, Android)\n- ✅ All existing desktop functionality verified working\n- ✅ Performance impact is minimal or negligible\n- ✅ Documentation updated with mobile support details\n\n### Dependencies\n- Completion of Milestones 1 and 2\n- Access to ~/.ensemble/metrics.db for agent analysis\n- Backend API access for agent recovery\n- Real mobile devices or comprehensive emulators for testing\n\n---\n\n## Risk Management\n\n### High Priority Risks\n1. **Agent errors require backend changes**: If BadRequestError is caused by backend API issues\n   - **Mitigation**: Document findings thoroughly, coordinate with backend team if needed\n2. **Bootstrap responsive system limitations**: If Bootstrap grid doesn't provide needed flexibility\n   - **Mitigation**: Use custom CSS media queries to supplement Bootstrap utilities\n\n### Medium Priority Risks\n1. **Touch targets remain too small**: Despite optimization efforts\n   - **Mitigation**: Test on real devices early, implement custom sizing if needed\n2. **Layout breaks on specific devices**: Device-specific rendering issues\n   - **Mitigation**: Test on multiple devices/emulators, implement device-specific fixes\n\n### Low Priority Risks\n1. **Performance degradation on mobile**: Responsive features impact load time\n   - **Mitigation**: Profile performance, optimize if issues arise\n\n## Success Metrics\n- **Mobile Responsiveness**: UI functions correctly on 320px-768px viewports\n- **Touch Usability**: All interactive elements meet 44x44px minimum tap target\n- **Agent Recovery**: 100% of high-priority failed agents resume successfully\n- **Compatibility**: Works on target mobile browsers (Safari iOS 14+, Chrome Android 90+)\n- **Performance**: No significant increase in load time or bundle size\n- **Functionality**: All existing desktop features remain working\n\n## Technical Approach\n- **Responsive Design**: Use Bootstrap's responsive utilities plus custom CSS media queries\n- **Mobile-First**: Implement responsive design with mobile-first approach\n- **Progressive Enhancement**: Ensure base functionality works, enhance for larger screens\n- **Agent Recovery**: Systematic analysis of error logs and configuration validation\n- **Testing Strategy**: Real device testing combined with developer tools emulation\n\n## Project Dependencies\n- Existing Ensemble UI React codebase\n- Bootstrap 5.x responsive framework\n- Python-based agent orchestration system\n- Access to system metrics and logs\n- Mobile testing environment"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011HSAueGJFQvexZEtAyTDMc', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_015821.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_015821.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01V2m5t6gUN4BnAcgiPWkRgR', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'd596f938', 'note': 'Created milestone plan with 3 phases: (1) Mobile UI Foundation & Responsive Layout, (2) Mobile UX Optimization & Navigation, (3) Agent System Recovery & Testing. Plan addresses both mobile responsiveness and agent recovery requirements.', 'category': 'milestone'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01V2m5t6gUN4BnAcgiPWkRgR', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)