{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:58:25", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-348b8389-5746-4a30-a79f-0e489e721533', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/brass_band_achievements_requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Brass Band Achievements System",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GQpzyH3f76vW3oUDezbiLU', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/brass_band_achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GQpzyH3f76vW3oUDezbiLU', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# British Brass Band Achievements - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** British Brass Band Achievements Expansion  \\n**Project ID:** 29b97d5e  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nExpand the existing Ensemble achievements system with a new \\"British Brass Band\\" category inspired by NABBA (North American Brass Band Association) and the British brass band tradition. These achievements celebrate the rich heritage of brass banding including competitions, sections, traditional instrumentation, and contest culture.\\n\\n## Background: NABBA & British Brass Bands\\n\\nNABBA (North American Brass Band Association) promotes British-style brass bands in North America since 1983. Key characteristics:\\n- **Contest Culture**: Championships with adjudicators scoring bands on test pieces\\n- **Section System**: Bands compete in divisions based on ability (Championship, Honor, Challenge, etc.)\\n- **Traditional Instrumentation**: Cornets, flugelhorn, tenor horns, baritones, euphoniums, trombones, tubas, percussion\\n- **Silver Band Tradition**: Many bands carry \\"Silver Band\\" in their name\\n- **Community Focus**: Youth bands, community bands, university bands\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Add New Category**: Create `BRASS_BAND` achievement category (parallel to existing `SKA` category)\\n2. **Achievement Content**: Add 10-15 British brass band themed achievements\\n3. **UI Updates**: Add brass band category to filter dropdown in AchievementsDashboard\\n4. **Maintain Consistency**: Follow existing achievement patterns for rarity, triggers, and points\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Backend Changes** (`src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`):\\n- Add `BRASS_BAND = \\"brass_band\\"` to `AchievementCategory` enum\\n- Add 10-15 new `Achievement` objects to the `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\\n- Include variety of rarities (common through legendary)\\n\\n**Frontend Changes** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`):\\n- Add brass_band category to filter dropdown with icon (\\ud83c\\udfba)\\n- Add brass_band to `getCategoryBadge` function\\n- Update \\"Brass/Band Facts\\" section or add separate fun facts\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- New API endpoints (using existing endpoints)\\n- Database schema changes (existing schema supports new category)\\n- New UI components beyond filter updates\\n\\n## Achievement Definitions\\n\\n### Theme Guidelines\\nBritish brass band achievements should reference:\\n- Contest/competition terminology (adjudicator, test piece, draw, sections)\\n- Instrumentation (cornets, euphoniums, tubas, percussion)\\n- Band traditions (Silver Bands, marching, community, youth development)\\n- Famous brass band pieces and composers\\n- Section rankings and promotions\\n- NABBA-specific events and culture\\n\\n### Proposed Achievements (10-15)\\n\\n| ID | Name | Description | Rarity | Points | Icon |\\n|----|------|-------------|--------|--------|------|\\n| `championship_section` | Championship Section | Achieved legendary status with 50+ successful tasks | LEGENDARY | 200 | \\ud83c\\udfc6 |\\n| `silver_band` | Silver Band | First agent to maintain 100% success rate across 5 tasks | RARE | 50 | \\ud83e\\udd48 |\\n| `principal_cornet` | Principal Cornet | Led 3+ sub-agents to successful completion in one task | UNCOMMON | 30 | \\ud83c\\udfba |\\n| `adjudicator` | The Adjudicator | Evaluated and passed judgment on 25+ test results | RARE | 60 | \\ud83d\\udccb |\\n| `test_piece` | Test Piece Mastery | Completed a particularly challenging task (>10 iterations) | UNCOMMON | 25 | \\ud83d\\udcdc |\\n| `bandroom_practice` | Bandroom Practice | Executed 10 tasks total (like rehearsal makes perfect) | COMMON | 15 | \\ud83c\\udfb5 |\\n| `promotion` | Section Promotion | Improved success rate from <50% to >90% | EPIC | 100 | \\u2b06\\ufe0f |\\n| `brass_section_harmony` | Brass Section Harmony | Multiple agents completed tasks simultaneously | RARE | 45 | \\ud83c\\udfb6 |\\n| `march_on_stage` | March on Stage | Completed first task of a new project | COMMON | 10 | \\ud83d\\udeb6 |\\n| `quick_march` | Quick March | Completed a task in under 10 seconds | RARE | 40 | \\u26a1 |\\n| `hymn_tune_encore` | Hymn Tune Encore | Recovered from failure and succeeded (like a well-loved encore) | UNCOMMON | 35 | \\ud83d\\ude4f |\\n| `grand_shield` | Grand Shield | Completed 25 consecutive successful tasks | EPIC | 120 | \\ud83d\\udee1\\ufe0f |\\n| `fanfare` | Fanfare | Triggered 5+ achievements in a single session | RARE | 55 | \\ud83d\\udcef |\\n| `youth_band_graduate` | Youth Band Graduate | New agent class completed its first 10 tasks | UNCOMMON | 20 | \\ud83c\\udf93 |\\n| `national_finals` | National Finals | Participated in project completion (full lifecycle) | LEGENDARY | 150 | \\ud83c\\udfc5 |\\n\\n### Achievement Implementation Details\\n\\n```python\\n# Example achievement definition pattern (for Development Manager reference)\\nAchievement(\\n    id=\\"silver_band\\",\\n    name=\\"Silver Band\\",\\n    description=\\"Maintained 100% success rate across 5 consecutive tasks - polished performance!\\",\\n    category=AchievementCategory.BRASS_BAND,\\n    rarity=AchievementRarity.RARE,\\n    icon=\\"\\ud83e\\udd48\\",\\n    points=50,\\n    agent_classes=[\\"*\\"],\\n    trigger_condition={\\"consecutive_successes\\": {\\"min\\": 5}}\\n)\\n```\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Existing Patterns**: Must follow existing achievement definition pattern\\n2. **Category Enum**: Add to existing `AchievementCategory` enum\\n3. **Frontend Consistency**: Match existing category badge/filter patterns\\n4. **Trigger Conditions**: Use existing trigger condition types where possible\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. \\u2705 `BRASS_BAND` category added to `AchievementCategory` enum\\n2. \\u2705 10-15 brass band achievements added to `ACHIEVEMENTS` list\\n3. \\u2705 Frontend filter dropdown includes brass_band with \\ud83c\\udfba icon\\n4. \\u2705 `getCategoryBadge` function handles brass_band category\\n5. \\u2705 All existing tests continue to pass\\n6. \\u2705 Achievements unlock correctly when conditions are met\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n### Backend File to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/achievements.py`\\n\\n### Frontend File to Modify\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx`\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Run existing achievement tests to ensure no regressions\\n- Manually verify brass_band filter works in UI\\n- Verify at least one achievement can be triggered\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n\\n1. **Icon Choice**: Using \\ud83c\\udfba (trumpet) as primary brass band icon since cornet emoji isn\'t widely available\\n2. **Trigger Conditions**: Reusing existing trigger types (consecutive_successes, total_executions, etc.)\\n3. **Points Balance**: Following existing points range (10-200) based on rarity\\n4. **No New Events**: Not adding new event types to activity tracker\\n\\n## Fun Facts for UI (Optional Enhancement)\\n\\nConsider adding to the fun facts section:\\n> **Did you know?** British-style brass bands date back to the early 1800s and originated in the industrial areas of Northern England. The standard brass band uses 25-30 players on cornets, horns, baritones, euphoniums, trombones, and tubas - no woodwinds allowed! The Black Dyke Band (founded 1855) is one of the oldest and most successful brass bands in the world. NABBA has been bringing this tradition to North America since 1983! \\ud83c\\udfba\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Implementation  \\n**Next Step:** Delegate to Development Manager for implementation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SEseXawfQYkNGYpHdMZNWz', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Brass Band Achievements System - Architecture Proposal\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### System Purpose\nExtend the existing Ensemble Achievements system with a new British Brass Band category, focusing on adding achievements that celebrate the rich heritage of brass banding.\n\n### Architecture Pattern\n- **Type**: Microservices-compatible Monolithic Architecture\n- **Pattern**: Layered Architecture with Clear Separation of Concerns\n- **Rationale**: Allows for easy extension while maintaining existing system integrity\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\n- **Framework**: Existing Ensemble framework\n- **Key Libraries**: \n  - `enum` for category management\n  - `typing` for type hinting\n- **Rationale**: \n  - Maintains consistency with existing codebase\n  - Provides strong typing and enum support\n  - Minimizes introduction of new dependencies\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React (existing implementation)\n- **State Management**: Context API or existing state management\n- **Styling**: Existing CSS framework\n- **Rationale**: \n  - Minimal changes required\n  - Leverages existing UI components\n  - Consistent user experience\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### Backend Components\n1. **Achievement Category Manager**\n   - Extends `AchievementCategory` enum\n   - Adds `BRASS_BAND` category\n   - Manages category-specific logic\n\n2. **Achievement Definition Service**\n   - Adds 10-15 new brass band achievements\n   - Maintains existing achievement definition structure\n   - Implements trigger conditions\n\n### Frontend Components\n1. **Achievements Dashboard**\n   - Updates category filter dropdown\n   - Adds brass band icon\n   - Renders brass band category achievements\n\n2. **Category Badge Component**\n   - Extends `getCategoryBadge` function\n   - Handles brass band category styling\n\n## D. File/Directory Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── runtime/\n│   └── agents/\n│       └── achievements.py        # Backend achievement definitions\n└── field/\n    └── ensemble_ui/\n        └── frontend/\n            └── src/\n                └── components/\n                    └── AchievementsDashboard.jsx  # Frontend updates\n```\n\n## E. Data Model\n\n### Achievement Definition Structure\n```python\nAchievement(\n    id=str,\n    name=str,\n    description=str,\n    category=AchievementCategory,\n    rarity=AchievementRarity,\n    icon=str,\n    points=int,\n    trigger_condition=Dict\n)\n```\n\n### Categories Enum\n```python\nclass AchievementCategory(Enum):\n    # Existing categories...\n    BRASS_BAND = "brass_band"\n```\n\n## F. API Design\n- **No New Endpoints Required**\n- Uses existing achievement tracking endpoints\n- Existing authentication and authorization mechanisms\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n- **Deployment Method**: Containerized deployment\n- **CI/CD**: Existing GitHub Actions workflow\n- **Environment**: Existing cloud infrastructure\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Testing\n- Test new achievement definitions\n- Verify trigger conditions\n- Validate category enum extension\n\n### Integration Testing\n- Test AchievementsDashboard updates\n- Verify category filter functionality\n- Ensure achievements unlock correctly\n\n## I. Alternatives Considered\n\n### Alternative 1: Microservices Achievement Service\n**Pros**: \n- Completely isolated achievement management\n- Independent scalability\n\n**Cons**:\n- Overcomplicates current system\n- Introduces unnecessary complexity\n- Higher operational overhead\n\n### Alternative 2: Completely New UI Component\n**Pros**:\n- Fresh design approach\n- More radical UI changes\n\n**Cons**:\n- Breaks existing UI consistency\n- More extensive development effort\n- Higher risk of user confusion\n\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\n\n1. **Risk**: Potential test failures\n   **Mitigation**: Comprehensive unit and integration testing\n\n2. **Risk**: Performance impact\n   **Mitigation**: Minimal changes, leverage existing infrastructure\n\n3. **Risk**: User confusion with new category\n   **Mitigation**: Clear UI indicators, consistent design\n\n## K. Open Questions / User Review Points\n\n1. Icon choice for brass band category\n2. Exact points allocation for achievements\n3. Specific wording for achievement descriptions\n\n## Recommended Action\nApprove this architecture proposal for implementation by the Development Manager.\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SEseXawfQYkNGYpHdMZNWz', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_015825.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_015825.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- Successfully conducted a comprehensive technical validation of the theme dropdown architecture. Applied systematic analysis across performance, security, scalability, and implementation feasibility di...\n- Successfully analyzed the UI theming requirements and designed a performance-focused architecture that balances maintainability with user experience. The proposal correctly identified CSS custom prope...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
