{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:58:27", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-0b7c3340-f030-4ecc-915a-9a6b1e0498a2', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Smart Task Decomposition Architecture Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TqokEZcURdGHk4zKz9rwMD', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TqokEZcURdGHk4zKz9rwMD', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Requirements Document\\n\\n## 1. Project Vision\\n\\nImplement a Smart Task Decomposition Engine that sits between user requests and the Ensemble AI execution pipeline. The system will transform high-level user requirements into optimized, dependency-aware execution plans that improve efficiency and cost-effectiveness.\\n\\n## 2. Core Objectives\\n\\n- **Intelligent Task Analysis**: Automatically analyze user requests to determine complexity, domain, and resource requirements\\n- **Optimized Decomposition**: Break complex tasks into 30-40 minute chunks with clear dependencies\\n- **Resource Optimization**: Select appropriate models (haiku/sonnet/opus) based on task complexity and budget constraints\\n- **Parallel Execution Planning**: Generate dependency-aware execution schedules with parallel wave grouping\\n- **User Approval Workflow**: Present plans via UI with approval/rejection/modification capabilities\\n- **Learning System**: Continuously improve estimates based on execution history\\n\\n## 3. Functional Requirements\\n\\n### 3.1 Task Decomposition Engine\\n- **TaskDecompositionEngine class** in `decomposition_engine.py`\\n- Methods: `analyze_task()`, `decompose_task()`, `generate_dependency_graph()`, `estimate_resources()`, `optimize_allocation()`, `generate_execution_schedule()`\\n- Support for multiple domains: \\"frontend\\", \\"backend\\", \\"fullstack_web_app\\"\\n- Complexity scoring (1-10 scale)\\n- Target duration: 30-40 minutes per subtask\\n\\n### 3.2 Data Models (Pydantic v2)\\n- `TaskAnalysis`: complexity_score, domain, estimated_human_hours, key_requirements\\n- `SubTask`: task_id, description, agent_type, estimated_duration_min, complexity, dependencies\\n- `DecompositionPlan`: task_analysis, sub_tasks, dependency_graph\\n- `ResourceEstimate`: agent_count, model_distribution, estimated_tokens, estimated_cost\\n- `AllocationPlan`: task_assignments, model_selections, resource_utilization\\n- `Schedule`: waves, total_duration, estimated_start_end_times\\n\\n### 3.3 Dependency Management\\n- Use NetworkX for DAG operations\\n- Validation rules: no cycles, connected components, valid dependencies\\n- Maximum depth: 10 levels, maximum parallel tasks: 8\\n- Topological sorting for wave generation\\n\\n### 3.4 Resource Optimization\\n- PuLP linear programming for task allocation\\n- Model selection strategy:\\n  - Simple tasks \\u2192 haiku ($0.25/1M tokens)\\n  - Moderate tasks \\u2192 sonnet ($3.00/1M tokens)\\n  - Complex tasks \\u2192 sonnet/opus ($15.00/1M tokens)\\n- Budget tier support with cost constraints\\n\\n### 3.5 Learning System\\n- **DecompositionLearner class** in `decomposition_learner.py`\\n- SQLite database for execution history\\n- Methods: `record_execution()`, `improve_estimates()`, `suggest_improvements()`\\n- Accuracy metrics tracking by domain and complexity\\n\\n### 3.6 API Integration\\n- **POST /api/decompose**: Accept user request, return decomposition plan\\n- **POST /api/approve-plan**: Handle user approval/rejection/modification\\n- **GET /api/decomposition-history**: Return accuracy metrics and recent executions\\n\\n### 3.7 Frontend Integration\\n- **TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx** React component\\n- Display Mermaid.js dependency graphs\\n- Show cost estimates and resource allocation\\n- Provide approve/reject/modify action buttons\\n- Interactive plan modification capabilities\\n\\n## 4. Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### 4.1 Performance Targets\\n- Total decomposition time: <5 seconds end-to-end\\n- Task analysis: <2 seconds (LLM response)\\n- Graph operations: <100ms\\n- Resource optimization: <500ms (LP solve)\\n\\n### 4.2 Scalability\\n- Support up to 100 subtasks per decomposition\\n- Handle parallel execution of up to 8 agents\\n- SQLite database adequate for learning history\\n\\n### 4.3 Reliability\\n- Graceful error handling for LLM failures\\n- Fallback to greedy allocation if LP infeasible\\n- Cycle detection with user feedback\\n- Input validation and sanitization\\n\\n### 4.4 Security\\n- Budget cap enforcement\\n- Plan integrity validation\\n- Rate limiting on history API\\n- Input sanitization before LLM processing\\n\\n## 5. Technical Stack\\n\\n- **Backend**: Python with Pydantic v2, NetworkX, PuLP, SQLite\\n- **Frontend**: React 18 with Mermaid.js visualization\\n- **API**: FastAPI integration with existing endpoints\\n- **Database**: SQLite for learning data storage\\n- **Testing**: TDD methodology with comprehensive test suite\\n\\n## 6. Integration Requirements\\n\\n### 6.1 Executive Director Integration\\n- New decomposition phase between requirements gathering and Development Manager spawning\\n- Extended output format with `decomposition_plan` field\\n- User approval workflow gate before execution\\n\\n### 6.2 Development Manager Integration\\n- Receive approved decomposition plans as input\\n- Execute tasks according to generated schedule\\n- Report actual execution metrics back to learning system\\n\\n## 7. File Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/agents/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_engine.py     # Core engine implementation\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_learner.py    # Learning and calibration\\n\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/backend/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 main.py                     # Updated with decomposition API endpoints\\n\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx # React UI component\\n\\ntests/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 test_decomposition.py       # Comprehensive test suite\\n```\\n\\n## 8. Success Criteria\\n\\n- System successfully decomposes complex tasks into optimal subtasks\\n- Users can visualize and approve execution plans before implementation\\n- Resource costs are accurately estimated within 20% margin\\n- Learning system improves estimate accuracy over time\\n- Integration with existing Executive Director and Development Manager workflows\\n- All tests pass using TDD methodology\\n\\n## 9. Out of Scope\\n\\n- Multi-LLM provider support (future extension)\\n- Real-time collaborative plan editing\\n- External integrations (JIRA, GitHub Issues)\\n- Custom decomposition strategies plugin architecture\\n\\n## 10. Assumptions\\n\\n- Existing Ensemble AI infrastructure supports agent spawning and communication\\n- FastAPI backend can be extended with new endpoints\\n- React frontend can integrate new components\\n- SQLite database is sufficient for learning data storage\\n- Users will actively participate in approval workflow"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent 