{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:58:28", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-62c54060-a719-4beb-a8b0-105538d0e7e4', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/continuation_requirements.md",\n  "project_name": "Ensemble UI Enhancement",\n  "project_id": "483a5b09",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011WdakotidugLcsJY9NWJph', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/continuation_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011WdakotidugLcsJY9NWJph', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Continuation of Unfinished Ensemble UI Enhancements\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\nThis document consolidates all unfinished requirements from the Ensemble UI project that need complete implementation including code, unit tests, and documentation.\\n\\n## Priority 1: Agent Completion Summary Visibility (CRITICAL)\\n\\n### Problem Statement\\nWhen agents complete, users cannot see what they accomplished without clicking through expandable sections. The completion summary, self_analysis, and deliverables data exists but is not exposed to the frontend.\\n\\n### Current State Analysis\\n- **Backend (main.py)**: Stores `result` in `active_agents[agent_id]` on completion (line ~233)\\n- **Activity Tracker**: `record_agent_completed()` stores result in activity data but does NOT extract summary/deliverables to agent_states\\n- **Frontend (App.jsx)**: Shows status badge but no summary text for completed agents\\n- **Frontend (ActivityFeed.jsx)**: Shows generic \\"completed\\" without summary\\n\\n### Required Changes\\n\\n#### 1. Backend: activity_tracker.py - `record_agent_completed()` \\n**Location**: `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` (~line 363)\\n\\n**Change**: Extract summary, self_analysis, deliverables from result and store in agent_states\\n\\n```python\\ndef record_agent_completed(\\n    self,\\n    agent_id: str,\\n    agent_name: str,\\n    request_id: str,\\n    result: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\\n):\\n    \\"\\"\\"Record agent completion.\\"\\"\\"\\n    # Existing activity recording...\\n    \\n    # ADD: Extract summary fields to agent_states for frontend access\\n    if agent_id in self.agent_states:\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"status\\"] = \\"completed\\"\\n        self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"completed_at\\"] = activity.timestamp\\n        \\n        # NEW: Extract key fields from result for UI display\\n        if result:\\n            self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"summary\\"] = result.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\")\\n            self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"self_analysis\\"] = result.get(\\"self_analysis\\", \\"\\")\\n            self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"deliverables\\"] = result.get(\\"deliverables\\", [])\\n            self.agent_states[agent_id][\\"message\\"] = result.get(\\"message\\", \\"\\")\\n```\\n\\n#### 2. Frontend: App.jsx - Agent Tasks Section\\n**Location**: `frontend/src/App.jsx` (~line 430-480 area where agent states are rendered)\\n\\n**Change**: Add summary display below completed agent status\\n\\n```jsx\\n{/* After status badge, add for completed agents: */}\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.summary && (\\n  <div style={{ \\n    fontSize: \'12px\', \\n    color: \'#9ca3af\', \\n    marginTop: \'6px\',\\n    padding: \'6px 8px\',\\n    backgroundColor: \'#1a1a2e\',\\n    borderRadius: \'4px\',\\n    borderLeft: \'3px solid #10b981\'\\n  }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcdd {state.summary.slice(0, 200)}{state.summary.length > 200 ? \'...\' : \'\'}\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n{state.status === \'completed\' && state.deliverables && state.deliverables.length > 0 && (\\n  <div style={{ fontSize: \'11px\', color: \'#6b7280\', marginTop: \'4px\' }}>\\n    \\ud83d\\udcc1 {state.deliverables.length} deliverable(s) created\\n  </div>\\n)}\\n```\\n\\n#### 3. Frontend: ActivityFeed.jsx - agent_completed case\\n**Location**: `frontend/src/components/ActivityFeed.jsx` - `renderActivityDetails` switch case\\n\\n**Change**: Show summary in collapsed view for agent_completed activities\\n\\n```jsx\\ncase \'agent_completed\':\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      {data.result?.summary && (\\n        <div style={{ marginBottom: \'8px\', color: \'#9ca3af\' }}>\\n          <strong>Summary:</strong> {data.result.summary}\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      {data.result?.deliverables?.length > 0 && (\\n        <div style={{ marginBottom: \'8px\' }}>\\n          <strong>\\ud83d\\udcc1 Deliverables:</strong> {data.result.deliverables.length} file(s)\\n          <ul style={{ margin: \'4px 0\', paddingLeft: \'20px\', fontSize: \'11px\' }}>\\n            {data.result.deliverables.slice(0, 5).map((d, i) => (\\n              <li key={i}>{d}</li>\\n            ))}\\n            {data.result.deliverables.length > 5 && (\\n              <li>...and {data.result.deliverables.length - 5} more</li>\\n            )}\\n          </ul>\\n        </div>\\n      )}\\n      {/* Existing expandable details... */}\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n```\\n\\n### Unit Tests Required\\n\\n#### Test: activity_tracker_test.py\\n```python\\ndef test_record_agent_completed_stores_summary():\\n    \\"\\"\\"Verify summary fields are extracted to agent_states on completion.\\"\\"\\"\\n    tracker = ActivityTracker()\\n    \\n    # Setup agent state\\n    tracker.agent_states[\\"test_agent\\"] = {\\"status\\": \\"running\\"}\\n    \\n    # Complete with result containing summary\\n    result = {\\n        \\"status\\": \\"success\\",\\n        \\"summary\\": \\"Implemented feature X with Y approach\\",\\n        \\"self_analysis\\": \\"Performance was good\\",\\n        \\"deliverables\\": [\\"file1.py\\", \\"file2.py\\"]\\n    }\\n    \\n    tracker.record_agent_completed(\\n        agent_id=\\"test_agent\\",\\n        agent_name=\\"test\\",\\n        request_id=\\"req123\\",\\n        result=result\\n    )\\n    \\n    state = tracker.agent_states[\\"test_agent\\"]\\n    assert state[\\"summary\\"] == \\"Implemented feature X with Y approach\\"\\n    assert state[\\"self_analysis\\"] == \\"Performance was good\\"\\n    assert state[\\"deliverables\\"] == [\\"file1.py\\", \\"file2.py\\"]\\n\\ndef test_record_agent_completed_handles_missing_summary():\\n    \\"\\"\\"Verify graceful handling when result has no summary.\\"\\"\\"\\n    tracker = ActivityTracker()\\n    tracker.agent_states[\\"test_agent\\"] = {\\"status\\": \\"running\\"}\\n    \\n    tracker.record_agent_completed(\\n        agent_id=\\"test_agent\\",\\n        agent_name=\\"test\\",\\n        request_id=\\"req123\\",\\n        result={\\"status\\": \\"success\\"}  # No summary\\n    )\\n    \\n    state = tracker.agent_states[\\"test_agent\\"]\\n    assert state.get(\\"summary\\", \\"\\") == \\"\\"\\n    assert state.get(\\"deliverables\\", []) == []\\n```\\n\\n#### Test: Frontend Component Tests\\n```jsx\\n// App.test.jsx additions\\ntest(\'renders summary for completed agent\', () => {\\n  const agentStates = {\\n    \'agent1\': {\\n      status: \'completed\',\\n      summary: \'Completed task successfully\',\\n      deliverables: [\'file1.py\', \'file2.py\']\\n    }\\n  };\\n  // Verify summary text is rendered\\n  // Verify deliverables count is shown\\n});\\n\\n// ActivityFeed.test.jsx additions\\ntest(\'shows summary in agent_completed activity\', () => {\\n  const activity = {\\n    activity_type: \'agent_completed\',\\n    data: {\\n      result: {\\n        summary: \'Task completed\',\\n        deliverables: [\'output.md\']\\n      }\\n    }\\n  };\\n  // Verify summary is visible without expansion\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n1. \\u2713 When agent completes, summary text visible in Agent Tasks section without clicking\\n2. \\u2713 Deliverable count shown with icon (\\ud83d\\udcc1 3 deliverables)\\n3. \\u2713 Activity Feed shows summary preview for agent_completed events\\n4. \\u2713 Graceful fallback when summary not available\\n5. \\u2713 Unit tests pass with >80% coverage for new code\\n6. \\u2713 No regressions in existing functionality\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Priority 2: Hide Completed Toggle Enhancement (PARTIALLY DONE)\\n\\n### Current State\\n- Toggle exists in App.jsx (`hideCompleted` state)\\n- NOT persisted to localStorage\\n- NOT available in ActivityFeed, GeneratedFiles panes\\n\\n### Required Changes\\n\\n#### 1. Add localStorage persistence\\n```jsx\\n// In App.jsx useEffect on mount\\nuseEffect(() => {\\n  const savedHideCompleted = localStorage.getItem(\'hideCompleted\');\\n  if (savedHideCompleted !== null) {\\n    setHideCompleted(savedHideCompleted === \'true\');\\n  }\\n}, []);\\n\\n// When toggle changes\\nconst handleHideCompletedChange = (e) => {\\n  const value = e.target.checked;\\n  setHideCompleted(value);\\n  localStorage.setItem(\'hideCompleted\', value.toString());\\n};\\n```\\n\\n#### 2. Add toggle to ActivityFeed component\\nPass `hideCompleted` prop and filter completed activities when enabled.\\n\\n#### 3. Add toggle to GeneratedFiles component\\nFilter files from completed agents when toggle is enabled.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Priority 3: Agent Invocation Context Display (FROM requirements.md)\\n\\n### Required Changes\\n1. Capture invocation context when agents spawn (activity_tracker)\\n2. Display invocation description in AgentHierarchyTree, AgentStatusPane, AgentSummaryPane\\n3. Show what task each agent was specifically invoked to accomplish\\n\\n### Implementation deferred to after Priority 1 completion\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Success Criteria for Full Completion\\n1. All Priority 1 changes implemented with tests\\n2. All Priority 2 changes implemented with tests  \\n3. Integration verified with live agent execution\\n4. No console errors or warnings\\n5. Documentation updated\\n6. Git commit with all changes\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx`\\n- `frontend/src/components/ActivityFeed.jsx`\\n- `frontend/src/components/GeneratedFiles.jsx` (Priority 2)\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n- `src/runtime/agents/tests/test_activity_tracker_summary.py`\\n- `frontend/src/components/ActivityFeed.test.jsx` (if not exists)\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CkQzQQv37i7ZVSzGxmzF9C', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Architecture Proposal: Ensemble UI Enhancement\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Purpose\nEnhance the Ensemble UI to improve agent completion visibility, state management, and user experience through targeted improvements in agent state tracking and frontend representation.\n\n### Architectural Pattern\n- **Frontend**: React with Hooks-based state management\n- **Backend**: Python runtime with enhanced activity tracking\n- **Architecture Style**: Event-driven, stateful component architecture\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React 17+ \n- **State Management**: React Hooks (useState, useEffect)\n- **Styling**: CSS-in-JS / Tailwind-like utility classes\n- **Key Libraries**:\n  - `localStorage` for persistent UI state\n  - React Testing Library for component tests\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\n- **Runtime**: Existing Ensemble agent execution framework\n- **Key Components**:\n  - `activity_tracker.py` for agent state management\n  - JSON-based state serialization\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### A. Backend Components\n1. **ActivityTracker**\n   - Responsibility: Track agent lifecycle and store detailed completion states\n   - Key Methods:\n     - `record_agent_completed()`\n     - Enhanced state storage with summary extraction\n   - State Schema:\n     ```python\n     agent_states = {\n         "agent_id": {\n             "status": "completed",\n             "summary": str,\n             "self_analysis": str,\n             "deliverables": List[str],\n             "completed_at": Timestamp\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n\n### B. Frontend Components\n1. **App.jsx**\n   - Global state management\n   - Agent state rendering\n   - Hide Completed toggle with localStorage persistence\n\n2. **ActivityFeed.jsx**\n   - Renders activity stream\n   - Supports filtering completed activities\n   - Displays agent completion summaries\n\n3. **AgentStatusPane**\n   - Displays individual agent status\n   - Shows completion summaries inline\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n```\nBackend (ActivityTracker)\n  ↓ Stores Detailed Agent State\nFrontend Components\n  ├── App.jsx (Global State)\n  ├── ActivityFeed (Rendering)\n  └── AgentStatusPane (Individual Agent View)\n```\n\n## 5. Feature Implementation Strategy\n\n### Agent Completion Visibility\n- **Backend**: Extract and store summary in `agent_states`\n- **Frontend**: Render summary conditionally based on agent status\n- **Visibility Levels**:\n  1. Truncated summary in main view\n  2. Expandable full details\n  3. Deliverables count and preview\n\n### Hide Completed Toggle\n- Persistent across sessions via `localStorage`\n- Applied to:\n  - Agent Tasks list\n  - Activity Feed\n  - Generated Files view\n\n## 6. Testing Strategy\n\n### Backend Tests\n- Unit tests for `activity_tracker.py`\n- Verify summary extraction\n- Test edge cases (missing data)\n- Validate state mutations\n\n### Frontend Tests\n- Component rendering tests\n- State management verification\n- Toggle behavior validation\n- Snapshot testing for UI components\n\n## 7. Deployment Considerations\n- No infrastructure changes required\n- Frontend rebuild and redeploy\n- Backend module update in agent runtime\n\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Performance Risks\n- **Risk**: Increased state management complexity\n- **Mitigation**: \n  - Limit summary length\n  - Lazy loading of full details\n  - Efficient React rendering with `useMemo`\n\n### Data Integrity Risks\n- **Risk**: Incomplete or malformed agent results\n- **Mitigation**: \n  - Defensive programming in `record_agent_completed()`\n  - Provide default/empty states\n  - Graceful rendering with fallback content\n\n## 9. Open Questions / Future Considerations\n- How to handle very long agent summaries?\n- Performance impact of storing more metadata\n- Future: More granular activity filtering\n\n## 10. Key Architectural Decisions\n1. Leverage existing `activity_tracker.py` for state management\n2. Use React Hooks for state and side effects\n3. Implement localStorage for UI state persistence\n4. Conditional rendering for agent summaries\n5. Minimal backend changes, focus on frontend enhancement\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CkQzQQv37i7ZVSzGxmzF9C', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_015814.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_015814.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013hx9MThKxHQnuzUAE633ri', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Ensemble UI Enhancement', 'description': 'Improve agent completion visibility and state management in the Ensemble UI with targeted frontend and backend enhancements.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013hx9MThKxHQnuzUAE633ri', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "62d7a1db", "message": "Created project: Ensemble UI Enhancement", "summary": {"project_id": "62d7a1db", "project_name": "Ensemble UI Enhancement", "description": "Improve agent completion visibility and state management in the Ensemble UI with targeted frontend and backend enhancements.", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T01:58:18.006705", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T01:58:18.006705", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T01:58:18.006705", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Ensemble UI Enhancement\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- Successfully conducted a comprehensive technical validation of the theme dropdown architecture. Applied systematic analysis across performance, security, scalability, and implementation feasibility di...\n- Successfully analyzed the UI theming requirements and designed a performance-focused architecture that balances maintainability with user experience. The proposal correctly identified CSS custom prope...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If