{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:58:37", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-e4833124-6a25-4bb5-87e7-b1ecabd15b45', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/decomposition_milestones.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0173DUQbPQo1dwH5e6HzvZJa', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Decomposition Milestones Implementation', 'description': 'Implement features specified in decomposition_milestones.md following TDD methodology'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0173DUQbPQo1dwH5e6HzvZJa', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "e377745c", "message": "Created project: Decomposition Milestones Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "e377745c", "project_name": "Decomposition Milestones Implementation", "description": "Implement features specified in decomposition_milestones.md following TDD methodology", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T01:57:03.869839", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T01:57:03.869839", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T01:57:03.869839", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Decomposition Milestones Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ra2TXGNBM1FK2cFNDE7PnD', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/decomposition_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ra2TXGNBM1FK2cFNDE7PnD', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Overview\\nTransform the Ensemble AI Executive Director from a simple coordinator into an intelligent planner with a Smart Task Decomposition Engine.\\n\\n## Milestone 1: Core Decomposition Engine (Priority)\\n**Objective**: Build the core TaskDecompositionEngine class with all essential methods.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_engine.py` - Core engine with:\\n  - `TaskDecompositionEngine` class\\n  - `analyze_task()` - Analyze task complexity and domain\\n  - `decompose_task()` - Break task into sub-tasks\\n  - `generate_dependency_graph()` - Create DAG using NetworkX\\n  - `estimate_resources()` - Calculate agent/cost/time estimates\\n  - `optimize_allocation()` - Linear programming for optimal allocation\\n  - `generate_execution_schedule()` - Create parallel execution waves\\n- Pydantic data models: TaskAnalysis, SubTask, DecompositionPlan, ResourceEstimate, AllocationPlan, Schedule\\n- Unit tests for core functionality\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Engine can analyze and decompose a complex task into valid DAG\\n- Resource estimates include agents, tokens, cost, and time\\n- Execution schedule produces valid parallel waves\\n- All tests pass\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Learning Module\\n**Objective**: Build the DecompositionLearner for continuous improvement.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_learner.py` - Learning module with:\\n  - `DecompositionLearner` class\\n  - `record_execution()` - Store actual vs. estimated performance\\n  - `improve_estimates()` - Calibrate estimates based on history\\n  - `suggest_improvements()` - Generate optimization suggestions\\n  - `get_historical_accuracy()` - Report on estimate accuracy\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Learning module integrates with existing metrics.py database\\n- Calibration improves estimates over multiple executions\\n- Accuracy metrics properly tracked\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: API Endpoints & Backend Integration\\n**Objective**: Add REST API endpoints for decomposition.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `POST /api/decompose` - Decompose a user request\\n- `POST /api/approve-plan` - Accept/reject/modify plan\\n- `GET /api/decomposition-history` - Get historical accuracy\\n- Integration with existing backend main.py\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All endpoints return correct JSON responses\\n- Error handling for invalid requests\\n- CORS configured properly\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1, Milestone 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Frontend Visualization\\n**Objective**: Build React component for task decomposition visualization.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx` component with:\\n  - Mermaid diagram rendering for dependency graph\\n  - Resource estimates display (agents, cost, time)\\n  - Execution wave visualization\\n  - Agent assignment table\\n  - Approve/Reject/Modify action buttons\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Component renders decomposition plans correctly\\n- User can approve/reject/modify plans\\n- Responsive design works on various screens\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 3\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 5: Testing & Documentation\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive test suite and documentation.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `tests/test_decomposition.py` - Full test suite:\\n  - Unit tests for each method\\n  - Integration tests for full flow\\n  - Graph validity tests (DAG, cycles)\\n  - Benchmark tests (simple/medium/complex)\\n  - Learning accuracy tests\\n- `TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md` - Documentation:\\n  - Architecture overview\\n  - Usage examples\\n  - API reference\\n  - Configuration options\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Test coverage > 80%\\n- All tests pass\\n- Documentation complete and accurate\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1-4\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n- Milestone 1: Core Engine - ~2-3 hours\\n- Milestone 2: Learning Module - ~1-2 hours\\n- Milestone 3: API Endpoints - ~1 hour\\n- Milestone 4: Frontend - ~1-2 hours\\n- Milestone 5: Testing & Docs - ~1-2 hours\\n\\n**Total Estimated Time**: ~6-10 hours of agent work\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014dSpX3g8EmWAhEgRHrctQR', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Requirements Document\n\n## Project Overview\n\n**Vision**: Transform the Ensemble AI Executive Director from a simple coordinator into an intelligent planner with a Smart Task Decomposition Engine.\n\n**Objective**: Build a sophisticated task decomposition system that analyzes complex user requests, breaks them into optimal sub-tasks, generates dependency graphs, estimates resources, and creates efficient execution schedules.\n\n## Core Requirements\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n**F1. Task Analysis & Decomposition**\n- System must analyze task complexity and domain\n- Break complex tasks into manageable sub-tasks\n- Generate directed acyclic graphs (DAG) for task dependencies\n- Support parallel execution planning\n\n**F2. Resource Management**\n- Estimate required agents, tokens, cost, and time for each sub-task\n- Optimize resource allocation using linear programming\n- Generate execution schedules with parallel waves\n- Support multiple agent types and specializations\n\n**F3. Learning & Improvement**\n- Record actual vs. estimated performance data\n- Continuously improve estimates based on historical data\n- Track accuracy metrics over time\n- Suggest optimization improvements\n\n**F4. API Integration**\n- Provide REST endpoints for decomposition operations\n- Support plan approval/rejection/modification workflows\n- Integrate with existing FastAPI backend\n- Maintain CORS compatibility\n\n**F5. User Interface**\n- Visualize dependency graphs using Mermaid diagrams\n- Display resource estimates and execution schedules\n- Provide interactive plan approval interface\n- Show agent assignments and timeline\n\n### Non-Functional Requirements\n\n**N1. Performance**\n- Decomposition analysis must complete within 5 seconds\n- Support concurrent decomposition requests\n- Maintain response time under 2 seconds for API calls\n\n**N2. Reliability**\n- System must handle invalid inputs gracefully\n- Provide meaningful error messages\n- Maintain data integrity across operations\n\n**N3. Scalability**\n- Support task graphs with up to 100 nodes\n- Handle multiple concurrent users\n- Efficient memory usage for large decompositions\n\n**N4. Maintainability**\n- Test coverage > 80%\n- Comprehensive documentation\n- Clean, modular architecture\n\n## Technical Specifications\n\n### Technology Stack\n- **Backend**: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic\n- **Dependencies**: NetworkX (graph operations), PuLP (optimization)\n- **Frontend**: React, Mermaid (diagram rendering)\n- **Database**: SQLite (existing metrics.py integration)\n- **Testing**: pytest\n\n### Data Models\n\n**TaskAnalysis**\n- task_id: str\n- complexity: str (simple|medium|complex)\n- domain: str\n- estimated_duration: float\n- confidence_score: float\n\n**SubTask**\n- sub_task_id: str\n- description: str\n- agent_type: str\n- dependencies: List[str]\n- estimated_resources: ResourceEstimate\n\n**DecompositionPlan**\n- plan_id: str\n- original_task: str\n- sub_tasks: List[SubTask]\n- dependency_graph: dict\n- total_estimate: ResourceEstimate\n- execution_schedule: Schedule\n\n### API Endpoints\n\n**POST /api/decompose**\n- Input: user request text\n- Output: DecompositionPlan JSON\n- Functionality: Analyze and decompose task\n\n**POST /api/approve-plan**\n- Input: plan_id, approval_status, modifications\n- Output: execution status\n- Functionality: Process plan approval/rejection\n\n**GET /api/decomposition-history**\n- Input: optional filters\n- Output: historical accuracy metrics\n- Functionality: Retrieve learning data\n\n### File Structure\n\n```\nsrc/runtime/agents/\n├── decomposition_engine.py     # Core TaskDecompositionEngine\n├── decomposition_learner.py    # Learning and improvement module\n\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/backend/\n├── main.py                     # Updated with new endpoints\n\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/\n├── TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx # React visualization component\n\ntests/\n├── test_decomposition.py       # Comprehensive test suite\n\ndocs/\n├── TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md      # Architecture and usage docs\n```\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n**Primary Success**\n- Core engine can decompose complex tasks into valid DAGs\n- Resource estimates are generated for all components\n- Learning module improves estimate accuracy over time\n- Frontend provides clear visualization and interaction\n- All tests pass with >80% coverage\n\n**Quality Gates**\n- No circular dependencies in generated graphs\n- Resource estimates within 20% accuracy after learning\n- API response times under 2 seconds\n- UI components are responsive and accessible\n- Complete documentation with examples\n\n## Assumptions\n\n**Technical Assumptions**\n- Existing Ensemble AI infrastructure is stable\n- FastAPI backend can handle additional endpoints\n- React frontend supports Mermaid diagram rendering\n- NetworkX library provides adequate graph operations\n\n**Business Assumptions**\n- Users will engage with decomposition plans before execution\n- Historical data will improve estimate accuracy\n- Linear programming approach is suitable for resource optimization\n- DAG structure is appropriate for task dependencies\n\n## Constraints\n\n**Time Constraints**\n- Implementation targeted for 6-10 hours of development work\n- Must integrate with existing system without breaking changes\n\n**Technical Constraints**\n- Must use existing database schema (metrics.py)\n- Frontend must maintain current design patterns\n- Backend must preserve existing API compatibility\n\n**Resource Constraints**\n- Development limited to specified agent capabilities\n- Must work within current infrastructure limits\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Real-time collaboration on decomposition plans\n- Advanced machine learning for task prediction\n- Integration with external project management tools\n- Automated task execution (only planning)\n- Multi-tenant support\n\n## Risk Analysis\n\n**High Risk**\n- Graph complexity causing performance issues\n- Learning algorithm convergence problems\n\n**Medium Risk**\n- Frontend rendering large dependency graphs\n- API integration compatibility issues\n\n**Low Risk**\n- Data model changes\n- Testing infrastructure setup\n\n## Implementation Methodology\n\n**Development Approach**: Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n1. Write tests first for each component\n2. Implement code to pass tests\n3. Refactor for optimization\n4. Integration testing between components\n\n**Quality Assurance**\n- Unit tests for all core methods\n- Integration tests for full workflows\n- Performance benchmarking\n- User acceptance testing for UI components'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014dSpX3g8EmWAhEgRHrctQR', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui