{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:58:40", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a501ef20-e4ae-4952-a588-973a89dae982', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Ensemble UI Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EYfSw49VmeGc9H1LyXLkHm', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EYfSw49VmeGc9H1LyXLkHm', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Requirements Document\\n\\n## 1. Project Vision\\n\\nImplement a Smart Task Decomposition Engine that sits between user requests and the Ensemble AI execution pipeline. The system will transform high-level user requirements into optimized, dependency-aware execution plans that improve efficiency and cost-effectiveness.\\n\\n## 2. Core Objectives\\n\\n- **Intelligent Task Analysis**: Automatically analyze user requests to determine complexity, domain, and resource requirements\\n- **Optimized Decomposition**: Break complex tasks into 30-40 minute chunks with clear dependencies\\n- **Resource Optimization**: Select appropriate models (haiku/sonnet/opus) based on task complexity and budget constraints\\n- **Parallel Execution Planning**: Generate dependency-aware execution schedules with parallel wave grouping\\n- **User Approval Workflow**: Present plans via UI with approval/rejection/modification capabilities\\n- **Learning System**: Continuously improve estimates based on execution history\\n\\n## 3. Functional Requirements\\n\\n### 3.1 Task Decomposition Engine\\n- **TaskDecompositionEngine class** in `decomposition_engine.py`\\n- Methods: `analyze_task()`, `decompose_task()`, `generate_dependency_graph()`, `estimate_resources()`, `optimize_allocation()`, `generate_execution_schedule()`\\n- Support for multiple domains: \\"frontend\\", \\"backend\\", \\"fullstack_web_app\\"\\n- Complexity scoring (1-10 scale)\\n- Target duration: 30-40 minutes per subtask\\n\\n### 3.2 Data Models (Pydantic v2)\\n- `TaskAnalysis`: complexity_score, domain, estimated_human_hours, key_requirements\\n- `SubTask`: task_id, description, agent_type, estimated_duration_min, complexity, dependencies\\n- `DecompositionPlan`: task_analysis, sub_tasks, dependency_graph\\n- `ResourceEstimate`: agent_count, model_distribution, estimated_tokens, estimated_cost\\n- `AllocationPlan`: task_assignments, model_selections, resource_utilization\\n- `Schedule`: waves, total_duration, estimated_start_end_times\\n\\n### 3.3 Dependency Management\\n- Use NetworkX for DAG operations\\n- Validation rules: no cycles, connected components, valid dependencies\\n- Maximum depth: 10 levels, maximum parallel tasks: 8\\n- Topological sorting for wave generation\\n\\n### 3.4 Resource Optimization\\n- PuLP linear programming for task allocation\\n- Model selection strategy:\\n  - Simple tasks \\u2192 haiku ($0.25/1M tokens)\\n  - Moderate tasks \\u2192 sonnet ($3.00/1M tokens)\\n  - Complex tasks \\u2192 sonnet/opus ($15.00/1M tokens)\\n- Budget tier support with cost constraints\\n\\n### 3.5 Learning System\\n- **DecompositionLearner class** in `decomposition_learner.py`\\n- SQLite database for execution history\\n- Methods: `record_execution()`, `improve_estimates()`, `suggest_improvements()`\\n- Accuracy metrics tracking by domain and complexity\\n\\n### 3.6 API Integration\\n- **POST /api/decompose**: Accept user request, return decomposition plan\\n- **POST /api/approve-plan**: Handle user approval/rejection/modification\\n- **GET /api/decomposition-history**: Return accuracy metrics and recent executions\\n\\n### 3.7 Frontend Integration\\n- **TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx** React component\\n- Display Mermaid.js dependency graphs\\n- Show cost estimates and resource allocation\\n- Provide approve/reject/modify action buttons\\n- Interactive plan modification capabilities\\n\\n## 4. Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### 4.1 Performance Targets\\n- Total decomposition time: <5 seconds end-to-end\\n- Task analysis: <2 seconds (LLM response)\\n- Graph operations: <100ms\\n- Resource optimization: <500ms (LP solve)\\n\\n### 4.2 Scalability\\n- Support up to 100 subtasks per decomposition\\n- Handle parallel execution of up to 8 agents\\n- SQLite database adequate for learning history\\n\\n### 4.3 Reliability\\n- Graceful error handling for LLM failures\\n- Fallback to greedy allocation if LP infeasible\\n- Cycle detection with user feedback\\n- Input validation and sanitization\\n\\n### 4.4 Security\\n- Budget cap enforcement\\n- Plan integrity validation\\n- Rate limiting on history API\\n- Input sanitization before LLM processing\\n\\n## 5. Technical Stack\\n\\n- **Backend**: Python with Pydantic v2, NetworkX, PuLP, SQLite\\n- **Frontend**: React 18 with Mermaid.js visualization\\n- **API**: FastAPI integration with existing endpoints\\n- **Database**: SQLite for learning data storage\\n- **Testing**: TDD methodology with comprehensive test suite\\n\\n## 6. Integration Requirements\\n\\n### 6.1 Executive Director Integration\\n- New decomposition phase between requirements gathering and Development Manager spawning\\n- Extended output format with `decomposition_plan` field\\n- User approval workflow gate before execution\\n\\n### 6.2 Development Manager Integration\\n- Receive approved decomposition plans as input\\n- Execute tasks according to generated schedule\\n- Report actual execution metrics back to learning system\\n\\n## 7. File Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/agents/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_engine.py     # Core engine implementation\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_learner.py    # Learning and calibration\\n\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/backend/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 main.py                     # Updated with decomposition API endpoints\\n\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx # React UI component\\n\\ntests/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 test_decomposition.py       # Comprehensive test suite\\n```\\n\\n## 8. Success Criteria\\n\\n- System successfully decomposes complex tasks into optimal subtasks\\n- Users can visualize and approve execution plans before implementation\\n- Resource costs are accurately estimated within 20% margin\\n- Learning system improves estimate accuracy over time\\n- Integration with existing Executive Director and Development Manager workflows\\n- All tests pass using TDD methodology\\n\\n## 9. Out of Scope\\n\\n- Multi-LLM provider support (future extension)\\n- Real-time collaborative plan editing\\n- External integrations (JIRA, GitHub Issues)\\n- Custom decomposition strategies plugin architecture\\n\\n## 10. Assumptions\\n\\n- Existing Ensemble AI infrastructure supports agent spawning and communication\\n- FastAPI backend can be extended with new endpoints\\n- React frontend can integrate new components\\n- SQLite database is sufficient for learning data storage\\n- Users will actively participate in approval workflow"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015p5un4gM1Arcsk61NyxiLj', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Ensemble UI Implementation', 'description': 'Smart Task Decomposition Engine implementation with task analysis, decomposition, and learning capabilities'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content':